window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201","paragraphs":["Returning the Favor (1)","I didn’t understand.","No matter how many times I thought it over, I simply couldn’t understand.","I had clearly heard that dragons treasured their young above all else.","In other words, they would never entrust their children to someone they didn’t trust.","If anything happened to the hatchling while it was here, I would face terrifying retaliation.","Moreover, this was the Forest of Four Seasons. Unless animals belonged to the same group, they were essentially enemies.","There was the kangaroo arena, which functioned as neutral territory, but that was an extremely rare exception founded upon an unspoken agreement.","The moment they left the neutral zone, they became enemies again. In other words, nowhere was truly safe.","\"Pibiiii~\"","\"Kyuuu~ Kyu~\"","So why had the dragon entrusted its hatchling to me?","The hatchling was currently running around and playing excitedly with Wonmo.","Whenever the hatchling took flight with a flap of its wings, Wonmo hopped up and down after it.","Watching the two adorable babies play together put my mind at ease, but that feeling didn’t last long.","\"Mister.\"","\"....\"","\"This is your first time seeing anything like this too, right? It’s my first time as well.\"","I had absolutely no idea how I was supposed to treat the hatchling.","Had the dragon genuinely mistaken this place for a daycare center and left its child with me, or was there some other reason?","Whatever the case, one thing was certain.","I had to protect the hatchling at all costs.","Only yesterday, it had crawled into the cave with wounds covering its entire body.","I didn’t know what had attacked it, but there was a high chance that threat was still nearby.","The dragon probably went to slaughter whatever did it.","Perhaps it had only entrusted the hatchling to me until that was done.","I released a long sigh and accepted reality.","I couldn’t drive the hatchling away, so we had no choice but to get along.","Fortunately, the hatchling seemed to like this place and played well with Wonmo.","\"Kyuuuuu~\"","\"Piiii~\"","Even now, they were using Largo’s neck as a slide.","Largo himself was sweating profusely as he nervously watched the hatchling’s every move.","Maybe this actually makes the shelter safer?","Dragons were terrifying.","And that fear seemed deeply engraved not only into humanity, but into all animals.","Just as Largo was doing now, most animals wouldn’t even consider laying a paw on the hatchling.","If so, the shelter might benefit from the same deterrent effect.","Of course, since this was the Forest of Four Seasons, there was no telling what sort of monstrous creature might appear.","It’s basically a living nuclear bomb.","That was genuinely how dragons were treated.","All-Father had once told me that a dragon heart alone possessed enough power to annihilate an entire city.","If even its heart held that much power, what about the creature carrying that heart?","There was no need to ask.","I silently watched the hatchling and Wonmo playing before accessing the Gallery.","I wanted to inform everyone about the current situation and, while I was at it, ask why the dragon might have left its hatchling with me.","Title: I opened a daycare center","Wild Grylls","(A photo of the hatchling playing with Wonmo)","(A video of the hatchling running around excitedly)","(A video of the hatchling struggling to drag Wonmo)","I don’t know why, but the dragon left its hatchling with me.","Does anyone know the reason? They originally left together, but then the dragon came back and dropped the hatchling off.","I thought dragons treasured their young. Does anyone know why it’s doing this?","└ Heavenly Demon: If it was willing to leave its young with you, it must trust you. In a way, that is only natural.","└ Wild Grylls: Why would it trust me?","└ Heavenly Demon: Did you not say dragons were as intelligent as humans? Moreover, unlike humans, beasts do not forget kindness or grudges.","└ Wild Grylls: Dumping a hatchling on me isn’t repaying a favor. It’s throwing a bomb at me;;","└ SwordMaster: Don’t look at it so negatively. In a sense, this means you have a dragon’s protection, doesn’t it?","└ A person under a dragon’s protection. Didn’t that appear in legends too?","└ Yeah, but that came from mythology. Those stories originated from when dragons ruled over humanity.","└ So the gods killed those dragons and liberated humanity?","└ That’s also true.","└ Why, though? To a kingdom protected by a dragon, wouldn’t the gods have seemed like invaders?","└ Starlight Princess: Because the dragons’ exploitation was so severe. That’s also where the legends about dragon lairs containing all manner of treasures originated.","└ Sounds like dragons had really shitty personalities, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: They weren’t particularly pleasant. There are even stories of them killing people with their breath whenever something displeased them. That dragon is relatively good-natured by comparison.","└ Aren’t you basically living on borrowed time, then?","└ Not even that. His life is hanging by a thread.","└ A thread hanging from another thread, lmaooo.","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly awful.","Most of them had reached the same conclusion as me.","Since I had protected its child, the dragon had judged this to be a safe place.","The problem was that dragons were generally ferocious by nature, so there was no telling when it might suddenly turn on me.","One way or another, it remained a ticking time bomb.","Ugh. I don’t know anymore.","I might as well eat. Worrying about it wouldn’t solve anything.","I would have to become as close to the hatchling as possible, making the dragon less willing to hurt me.","Before that, I decided to give it a name.","I couldn’t keep calling it \"the hatchling\" every time.","If I ask the Gallery, they’ll only suggest all kinds of ridiculous names.","From now on, I would choose the names myself.","As it happened, a suitable name had already come to mind.","A species that had once conquered Earth before going extinct after a great cataclysm.","And the most famous name associated with that species.","Recalling that name, I approached the hatchling.","Then I lifted the hatchling, which had been playing excitedly with Wonmo, and spoke.","\"Tyranno.\"","\"Pii?\"","\"Your name is Tyranno now. Got it?\"","\"Pii!\"","Now that I had named it, it was time to put it down.","It would take some time for it to recognize its own name, but that was fine.","I was about to start preparing our meal when—","\"...Tyranno?\"","Ludwig asked with a slightly bewildered expression.","He apparently hadn’t imagined that I would go so far as to name it.","\"Yes. We’ll probably be seeing a lot of it from now on, so it needs a name.\"","Ludwig nodded silently.","I was the owner of this place, so he seemed to respect my decision.","\"I’m going upriver for now. Please stay here.\"","Carrying Fast Sloth on my back, I headed upriver and left Ludwig at the shelter.","Someone of Ludwig’s strength would be more than capable of defending it, and Kkobong was there too.","\"By the way, weren’t you afraid of the dragon?\"","I asked Fast Sloth as we made our way upstream.","Everyone else had been terrified by the dragon, but Fast Sloth had leisurely scratched his back.","I couldn’t tell whether he was brave or simply incapable of feeling fear.","Naturally, Fast Sloth didn’t answer me. As always, his expression remained relaxed.","I wished he could speak like the gorillas.","Did he even have vocal cords in the first place? Still, at least he could understand me, so it was fine.","Roooooar!","Perhaps because the rain had stopped some time ago, the river had returned to its normal level.","There weren’t any fish lying scattered around the riverbank either. The animals had probably carried them away.","I had originally planned to come upriver first thing in the morning, but the dragon’s sudden appearance had made that impossible.","I’ll just set the fish traps.","It hadn’t rained heavily yesterday, so there was no need to erect any stone barriers.","I quickly set the traps and returned to the shelter.","When I arrived, I was greeted by an amusing sight.","\"Chirp! Chirp! Chirp!\"","\"Chirp! Chirp!\"","While I was upriver, Ludwig seemed to have planted wheat seeds in the field.","The wheat soon began growing at a tremendous rate, naturally attracting a flock of birds.","Under normal circumstances, they would have stripped the entire field bare.","\"Piiiiik!\"","\"Chiiiiirp!\"","\"Chirp, chirp, chirp!\"","Flap-flap-flap!","But the instant Tyranno roared, the entire flock fled in a panic.","Despite being only a baby, he apparently possessed the natural intimidation of a dragon.","Thanks to him, Ludwig harvested the wheat without suffering any interference.","\"Oh?\"","That was unexpected.","If this continued, harvesting wheat would become much easier from now on.","Ludwig must have reached the same conclusion, because he looked at Tyranno with a peculiar expression.","Tyranno paid him no attention and immediately became absorbed in playing with Wonmo again.","\"Come on, you two. Eat before you go back to playing.\"","First, we needed to eat.","As I had mentioned before, we still had some fish left.","The problem was that Tyranno could easily devour an entire fish by himself.","There were five of us: me, Ludwig, Wonmo, Kkobong, and Tyranno.","We consumed five whole fish with every meal.","Fortunately, Largo only ate grass. Otherwise, the situation would have been horrifying.","I’ll either have to install more traps or expand the fields.","There was something else that concerned me.","Would Wonmo and Tyranno become picky eaters?","Wonmo was a bear and therefore omnivorous, but Tyranno was most likely a carnivore.","Unless Tyranno’s mother started delivering meat to us, I would have to ration our food for the time being.","Plump—","Once we had finished eating, I noticed a slight change in Wonmo.","He had visibly put on weight.","It wasn’t just his stomach that had become rounder; his overall size had increased.","That probably meant winter would arrive soon.","We had already prepared for it, but what would happen to Tyranno?","Would his mother take him away herself, or would she continue leaving him here?","\"Kyuuuuu.\"","Now that his belly was full, Wonmo toddled into the cave for a nap.","Tyranno blocked his path, apparently wanting to continue playing, but the difference in their sizes was too great.","Even when Tyranno blocked him with his body and tried pulling him back with his mouth, Wonmo didn’t budge.","\"Piiiiing....\"","When Wonmo eventually settled down for his nap, Tyranno looked heartbroken.","As if asking why Wonmo was sleeping when they could still play, he repeatedly pressed down on him with his forepaws.","But Wonmo had already departed for dreamland.","There was no waking him now.","Doesn’t this one sleep?","As far as I knew, most baby animals spent more than half the day asleep.","Dragons must have been an exception, because Tyranno was still brimming with energy.","I watched the dejected Tyranno before casually asking,","\"Tyranno, do you want to play with me?\"","\"Pii?\"","Flap! Flap!","Did he understand human speech too?","The moment I spoke to him, he began flapping his tiny wings.","Even his large eyes sparkled with excitement. Apparently, he was desperate to play.","Come to think of it, don’t dragons like shiny things?","I asked Tyranno to wait for a moment and opened a box.","Inside was the mithril left over from the incident involving Ludwig’s prosthetic leg.","Mithril was a material that glowed green, so perhaps Tyranno would like it.","I’ll roll it around for him to chase.","I took out a fist-sized piece of mithril shaped like a ball.","When I showed it to Tyranno, his expression immediately filled with curiosity.","Just as expected, dragons loved shiny things—","\"Chomp!\"","\"...?\"","Crunch! Crack! Crunch!","—though perhaps he loved them in a different sense.","Tyranno swallowed the mithril in one bite and chewed it with great relish.","Mithril was renowned for being as hard as steel, yet he was eating it like a cracker.","Gulp!","\"Piiii~\"","\"Was it tasty?\"","\"Pii!\"","As long as he enjoyed it, I supposed it was fine.","***","Dragons were widely known as the strongest living creatures on earth.","They possessed immense strength born from their overwhelming size.","They had minds intelligent enough to wield magic like humans.","They had wings that allowed them to soar freely through the sky.","Finally, they possessed breath attacks capable of melting everything in their path.","Very few beings could fight such creatures on equal footing.","That was why humans and most animals feared incurring a dragon’s wrath.","Most creatures ignored hatchlings as though they didn’t even exist. If anyone harmed one, that individual would be exiled from their group.","Expelling one member was preferable to having the entire group annihilated for the offense.","But that only applied outside the Forest of Four Seasons.","The Forest of Four Seasons was home to monsters every bit as terrifying as dragons.","There were already creatures that seemed to belong in a kaiju film, like the giant crab and giant crayfish Grylls had encountered at the lake.","In other words, monsters comparable to dragons in both size and strength existed here.","\"Grrrrrr.\"","The gray dragon released a terrifying growl as it glared ahead.","Its expression was murderous, as though it intended to tear apart the creature before it at any moment.","The dragon was currently inside none other than its own lair—its home.","Under normal circumstances, it would have rested there, but something prevented it from doing so.","Rustle—","An enormous white serpent had brazenly occupied the lair.","It radiated a different kind of oppressive presence from the dragon, while its flickering tongue seemed to be taunting its opponent.","The monster was more than twice the dragon’s length.","Its bulk was equally astounding. If it opened its jaws wide, it looked capable of swallowing the dragon whole.","It wasn’t one of the imoogi commonly found in the Central Plains.","It appeared to be a far superior creature.","\"Shaaaaa...!\"","When the enormous white serpent opened its mouth, a pair of razor-sharp venomous fangs came into view.","Purple liquid dripped from them toward the ground.","Sssssss!","No—it didn’t seep into the ground.","Even solid rock melted the instant the venom touched it.","This monster was the reason the dragon had been forced to leave its hatchling unattended.","It was also the reason the dragon had no choice but to entrust its hatchling to Grylls for a time.","Like the sky whale, it was a monstrous creature that should only have existed during the Mythological Age.","\"Graaaaaaaaah!\"","\"Shaaaaaaaaa!\"","In one corner of the Forest of Four Seasons, a life-or-death struggle began."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202","paragraphs":["Returning the Favor (2)","The sight of a dragon effortlessly chewing through mithril made me wonder whether an accident might happen soon.","Tyranno might think he was biting gently, only to tear off chunks of flesh.","The risk was especially high because Tyranno often played with Wonmo.","Fortunately, Wonmo had already learned to control his strength while playing with the raccoons.","For both their sakes, Tyranno needed to learn the same lesson.","\"Tyranno, bite me here.\"","\"Bebi?\"","With Tyranno perched on my shoulder, I pointed at my forearm.","He closely examined the spot I was pointing at, seemingly focused.","\"Bite down slowly until I say it hurts. Like this. Chomp!\"","When I mimed biting my forearm, Tyranno tilted his head.","Rather than explaining it verbally, I decided to demonstrate.","It was fine if he wanted to nibble us as a sign of affection, but his bite was far too powerful.","He needed to learn how to bite gently before an accident occurred.","In other words, I needed to teach him restraint and drill it into him.","\"Pii!\"","Tyranno apparently understood what I meant, because he smiled brightly and bit my forearm.","Crunch!","\"Aaaaaaargh! No! No, that’s not it! Let go! Let go!\"","\"Pipi?!\"","The moment he bit down, my bone nearly snapped.","I hurriedly stopped Tyranno, and he immediately pulled away upon hearing my scream.","When I examined my forearm, I found a distinct set of teeth marks.","How did it leave only marks? It wouldn’t have been strange if his teeth had pierced straight through.","My bone hadn’t broken, but the area was badly bruised.","I would probably have to inject some elixir into it soon.","\"See? Your bite is that strong. You mustn’t bite your friends so hard.\"","\"Piiii....\"","\"It’s okay. It’s okay. Mistakes happen. Come on, let’s try again.\"","Through consistent repetition, Tyranno quickly learned how to control his strength.","His intelligence was so high that he seemed to grasp exactly what I wanted.","Now that I no longer needed to worry about any accidents, only one concern remained.","How am I going to manage our food?","With another mouth to feed, our food shortage had become an urgent problem.","Largo could survive on leaves, but the other animals couldn’t.","Every last one of them is a glutton.","To make matters worse, winter was just around the corner.","I needed to stockpile enough food to survive it.","Potatoes were one of the most obvious foods to store for winter.","GrowGrowGrow had given me seed potatoes, so I only needed to plant them.","...Should I make kimchi too?","The pointless thought crossed my mind, but I immediately dismissed it.","Who had time to make kimchi in a situation like this? I didn’t even eat much kimchi to begin with.","It seemed best to search through the Gallery.","If I couldn’t find the answer, I could always ask someone.","Oh... Bread is an option too.","I quickly found several foods suitable for winter storage.","There was the smoked meat I had previously made by salting it, as well as salted vegetables.","Rice and wheat were said to be particularly suitable for surviving winter. Both simply needed to be stored somewhere cool.","For now, I planned to ask GrowGrowGrow for help.","If they didn’t have any, I would have to search the auction house for seeds.","There are also cabbages, spinach, radishes, and potatoes, but....","Trying to store too many different foods might only make things confusing.","Let’s survive this winter on wheat, potatoes, and sweet potatoes. In that case....","I needed to learn how to harvest wheat.","Rather than searching for the information myself, I asked GrowGrowGrow. That seemed much faster.","GrowGrowGrow: Once you’ve harvested the wheat, you need to dry it within four hours. Otherwise, its quality will deteriorate.","Wild Grylls: What happens if I don’t?","GrowGrowGrow: It’ll either rot or grow mold, won’t it?","Wild Grylls: ;;","I had originally planned to make bread from wheat flour.","However, after hearing the explanation, I gave up.","There was simply far too much work involved. Noodles would be much easier than bread.","Even producing the flour itself took a long time.","Come to think of it, bakers exist, but there isn’t a profession dedicated solely to cooking rice.","Since I had cooked rice at home every day, I had assumed making bread would be just as manageable.","But just as turning rice into rice cakes was difficult, baking bread was no simple task either.","So I changed my plan from wheat to rice.","GrowGrowGrow didn’t have any rice seeds, so I planned to ask someone else.","I can ask the Heavenly Demon, right?","Since the Central Plains came from a martial-arts world, there was a high chance that rice was available there.","I handed some soil over to GrowGrowGrow and contacted the Heavenly Demon.","Heavenly Demon: You are asking this one for rice?","Wild Grylls: Rice seeds, to be precise. I’m planning to grow it myself.","Heavenly Demon: Very well. This one shall have a close aide procure some for you.","Wild Grylls: Thank you.","Now that I would soon receive rice seeds from the Heavenly Demon, I decided to dry the wheat first.","I needed to thresh it before drying it, but removing every grain by hand would be incredibly difficult.","Therefore, I needed a threshing tool.","Since I would soon be harvesting rice as well, it wasn’t optional but essential.","A threshing tool is one thing, but I’ll also have to remove the husks.... Did farmers really do all this work by hand?","My respect for farmers suddenly began soaring.","I searched the auction house for threshing and husking tools.","\"Isn’t this a comb?\"","I found a threshing tool that looked somewhat like a comb.","More precisely, it was a comb-shaped piece of iron.","I purchased it and examined its construction. It was roughly the size of a person’s head.","I insert the heads of the grain between these teeth and pull, right?","One look was enough to understand how it worked.","So, what should I do next?","Make Ludwig do it, of course.","Before that, I spread a cloth over the ground.","Then I placed a chair at its edge and secured the threshing tool on top of it.","\"Come on. Let’s get to work.\"","\"Mm.\"","Rattle-rattle-rattle!","We inserted the wheat heads between the densely packed teeth and pulled.","Plump, appetizing grains showered onto the cloth.","Lick. Lick.","\"Hey, Tyranno! You can’t eat that!\"","\"Pii?\"","Tyranno tried licking up a few grains in the middle of our work, but I barely managed to stop him.","Afterward, we diligently threshed all the wheat we had harvested so far.","We gathered the separated grains and placed them somewhere that received plenty of sunlight.","Drying them like chili peppers should work.","I didn’t forget to apply insect repellent either.","The birds... won’t come back, right?","The birds had fled from Tyranno’s intimidating presence long ago.","At least while Tyranno was here, they probably wouldn’t return.","So, what should I do while waiting for the grain to dry?","\"Ludwig, I’m going out to scout the area.\"","\"Mm.\"","I headed out to hunt while conducting reconnaissance.","Ludwig should be more than capable of defending the shelter.","Besides, Kkobong was there with him.","Kkobong was also diligently using the threshing tool.","After all, we couldn’t survive the entire winter on nothing but rice and noodles.","I had originally intended to leave Tyranno behind as well.","\"Piiii! Piiii!\"","\"I told you, I’ll only be gone for a little while.\"","\"Piiii! Piiiiii!\"","But he clung to me, demanding that I stay—or take him with me if I insisted on leaving.","He was ridiculously strong.","Left with no choice, I decided to bring Tyranno along on the scouting trip.","Fast Sloth was already clinging to my back.","\"Do you really have to sit there?\"","\"Pii!\"","\"Fine. Do whatever you want.\"","Tyranno settled on top of my head as though it were a nest.","He was slightly heavy, but it wasn’t uncomfortable. It was better than letting him wander around and get lost.","Moreover, bringing him along produced an unexpected benefit: his reactions.","\"Pii.\"","Tyranno raised his head and cried softly, as though sensing something in a particular direction.","I was slightly skeptical, but I headed where he wanted me to go.","\"Oink.\"","\"Oh...?\"","There was a wild boar.","A wild boar comparable in size to a bus.","Its enormous, movie-monster-like body and sharply protruding tusks were particularly striking.","...I saw something like that in the military once, didn’t I?","The memory remained vivid even now.","A wild boar had wandered over while we were working.","There had been a jeep right next to it, yet that miraculous boar had somehow made the vehicle look small.","\"Oiiiiink!\"","A boar far larger than that one charged at me.","I had more or less expected this, so I was about to calmly move out of the way when—","\"Piaaaaaak!\"","Tyranno released an adorable roar from atop my head.","It had worked on the birds, but I wondered whether it would work on a wild boar.","\"Oink?!\"","Screeeeech!","It worked.","Extremely well, in fact.","The moment the boar heard Tyranno’s roar, its eyes widened and it slammed on the brakes.","I didn’t know whether it had recognized him as a hatchling or whether the fear of dragons was simply engraved into its instincts.","One thing was certain: a tremendous opportunity had presented itself.","Seizing the moment, I charged at the boar.","Crunch!","The Heavenly Demon’s sword sank directly into the boar’s forehead.","With its brain reduced to mush, the boar convulsed for a while before collapsing limply.","Thud!","Its body was so enormous that the ground trembled slightly when it fell.","I released the breath I had been holding and stared at the fallen boar.","It was so massive that this one carcass might be enough to last us through the winter.","Of course, I would need to build a large storage room.","Fortunately, I had plenty of ice.","\"...You’re incredible, aren’t you?\"","\"Pii!\"","When I stroked his chin and praised him, Tyranno proudly raised his head.","He seemed to be boasting, See how amazing I am!","It was still adorable, though.","I tightly bound the boar with the rope I had prepared.","There was no way I could carry something this large, so I planned to drag it back.","Still... this is pretty heavy.","That was inevitable, considering its size.","I just had to think of it as our winter food supply.","Just in case, I placed Tyranno on top of the boar and had him keep watch in every direction.","There were far too many thieves in the Forest of Four Seasons to do otherwise.","\"Kyu?\"","When I returned while dragging the boar, Wonmo greeted us after waking from his nap.","Ludwig and Kkobong were still threshing the wheat.","Despite having left only a short while ago, I had returned with an enormous haul.","\"Mister! You know how to butcher animals too, right?\"","\"#%$#\"","\"Then please help me.\"","Butchering this thing alone would take far too long.","Considering its sheer size, I wasn’t even sure I could butcher it properly.","Fortunately, Ludwig appeared quite skilled at it.","Perhaps his countless missions had often forced him to survive on his own.","\"One, two! Pull!\"","\"Hup!\"","\"Gwoong.\"","Despite preparing ourselves, even the preliminary work was difficult.","It reminded me of the saber-toothed tiger.","Butchering normally began by hanging the carcass upside down, which made it easier to drain the blood.","The problem was that the boar was so enormous that even suspending it upside down was difficult.","We enlisted Largo’s help.","He was remarkably strong and managed to hoist the boar to the desired height.","He was essentially a living crane.","I had never expected to use him this way, though.","Trickle, trickle—","Draining all the blood would take some time, so I began constructing a storage room while we waited.","It wasn’t a traditional icehouse, but something closer to a freezer.","It wouldn’t be used to store tools or miscellaneous supplies. It was exclusively for food.","My ability allowed me to produce a nearly unlimited supply of ice, so sufficient insulation would be enough.","I need to make sure the heat can escape properly... Wait, I’m short on sand again?","Whenever I obtained one thing, I discovered that I needed another. Then, once I acquired that, something else would be missing.","It felt as though I had fallen into an endless cycle.","Still, this was only natural.","It might have been different if I lived alone, but as our numbers increased, so did the number of things we needed.","I have enough time. Still, I should hurry.","I traveled downstream to gather sand, returned, and continued building the storage room.","After thoroughly coating the interior with soil and straw for insulation, I resumed butchering the boar.","I wanted to make Kkobong do it, but unfortunately, he was a gorilla.","The structure of his hands made them poorly suited to delicate work like butchering.","Crackle!","Once we had made sufficient progress with the butchering, I placed ice inside the storage room.","After filling it with ice, we stored the butchered boar, grain, vegetables, and everything else that could serve as food.","I’ll cover the entrance with cloth for now. I don’t have enough time to install a proper door.","By the time we finished everything, it was four thirty in the afternoon.","If I had worked alone, I wouldn’t have finished today.","An extra pair of hands truly made an enormous difference.","\"Good work. Would you like to wash up?\"","\"Mm.\"","I prepared bathwater for Ludwig, who had worked harder than anyone else today.","For the record, I planned to wash all the animals, including Kkobong.","Surprisingly, Kkobong was perfectly capable of washing himself. As long as I prepared his bathwater, he took care of everything on his own.","Largo only needed to be brushed and wiped down with a damp cloth.","Finally, there was Tyranno.","\"Piiii! Piiii!\"","\"What’s wrong? You don’t want a bath?\"","\"Piiii! Pii! Piiii!\"","As if he really were a cat, he vehemently refused to wash.","But for the sake of cleanliness, there was no helping it.","I had to bathe him.","He might not have fur, but there was no telling what kind of ticks might be hiding on his body.","\"You won’t get dinner if you don’t take a bath.\"","\"...Piiiing.\"","Fortunately, the threat of withholding food made him obedient.","And so, another uneventful day came to an end."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203","paragraphs":["Returning the Favor (3)","While Tyranno was settling in well at Grylls’s shelter—","Boooom! Bang!","The dragon had been locked in a life-or-death struggle with the enormous white serpent all day long.","The giant white serpent was every bit as formidable as its size and imposing presence suggested.","Its maw was large enough to swallow even the dragon whole.","Its venom could melt solid stone.","Its scales and hide could effortlessly withstand most attacks.","And despite its enormous bulk, it was remarkably agile.","With all these traits combined, the battle between them was a true clash of equals.","It was a battle between the dragon, the strongest creature on land, and a white serpent that rivaled it.","Their life-or-death struggle showed no sign of ending anytime soon.","Booooom!!!","At last, the white serpent collapsed with more than half its neck torn apart, bringing the long battle to an end.","The fight had lasted for more than half a day.","And the serpent’s neck was far from its only grievous injury.","One of its eyes had been gouged out, and its massive mouth had been ripped apart, leaving its jaw hanging loosely.","Just as the white serpent had opened its maw wide to bite, the dragon had seized the opportunity and shattered its jaw.","\"Grrrrr... Rrrr...\"","But the dragon was hardly in good condition either.","As befitted a battle between evenly matched foes, its body was covered in wounds both large and small.","The most serious injury was to its foreleg.","Its right foreleg had been completely torn off, and blood poured from the stump.","Its wings were no better. They had been shredded so badly that flight was impossible.","But even more dangerous than its wounds was the venom.","The white serpent’s venom was lethal even to a dragon, leaving it in a state where simply enduring was difficult.","\"Grrrr...\"","After checking several times to make sure the white serpent was truly dead, the dragon turned its head.","It looked in the direction of its hatchling—the child for whom it would gladly sacrifice its own life.","But if it tried to travel there now, its strength would fail completely and it would die.","It wanted to rush there immediately, but the dragon suppressed the urge.","Its hatchling was safe.","’...Please.’","The dragon slowly closed its eyes, beginning its recovery in earnest.","No creature could survive in this savage wilderness without the help of its parents.","That was why it had temporarily entrusted its hatchling to Grylls. For reasons it did not understand, the human had protected its child.","If he harmed the hatchling... it would not be too late to take revenge afterward.","Possessing an intellect no less keen than a human’s, the dragon had chosen to gamble on the better odds.","Rustle—","The dragon’s eyes gradually closed.","Its severed foreleg and shredded wing membranes slowly began to regenerate.","It would take at least several days for it to fully recover.","Praying inwardly that its hatchling would remain safe until then, the dragon finally closed its eyes completely.","’Come to think of it, that human...’","Just before its consciousness sank into the depths, the dragon recalled him.","That strangely alien human.","It had no idea why such a human was in this forest.","’Once I wake up, I should speak... with him...’","With that final thought, the dragon’s consciousness faded completely.","And though the dragon had fallen into a deep sleep—","Crack! Craaack!","Its body continued to heal.","***","Day 33 of survival.","I had spent the entire day working, so the hours flew by before I knew it.","In the evening, I also received rice seeds from the Heavenly Demon. Other than that, nothing particularly noteworthy happened.","When I woke up the next morning, I wondered whether Tyranno’s mother had arrived, but no one was there.","Instead, we were greeted by weather that was slightly cooler than before.","\"Kyuuu~ Kyuuu~\"","\"Piiiii! Pii!\"","Even with the cooler weather, the little ones were too busy playing to care.","There was one thing different from yesterday.","A ball.","Wonmo and Tyranno were both having the time of their lives playing with something resembling a soccer ball.","’I tossed it to them just in case, and they’re having a blast.’","Naturally, I had asked Cheonggu Princess for the soccer ball.","She gave me one that looked fairly expensive.","And her condition was incredibly simple: upload a photo or video of the two playing with it.","I had already planned to film them playing anyway.","’But first, I should make them some goalposts.’","I roughly assembled the goalposts out of wood. There was no need to put too much care into making them.","Then I explained the rules to Wonmo and Tyranno.","They were very simple: whoever got the ball between the goalposts scored.","\"Kyuuu!\"","\"Piiiik! Piiik!\"","The two began playing excitedly. I photographed and filmed them just as they were.","The sight alone was enough to fill me with warmth.","Now I was even more curious about how the gallery would react.","Title: Wonmo and Tyranno Are Playing Soccer","Wild Grylls","(A photo of Wonmo enthusiastically kicking the ball)","(A photo of Tyranno enthusiastically kicking the ball)","(A video of Wonmo dribbling the ball and scoring a goal)","(A video of Tyranno slamming his forepaws against the ground in frustration)","Princess Cheonggu, thank you so much for being a princess.","The kids are having a great time thanks to you!","└ Heavenly Demon: Children must grow through play. What a heartwarming sight.","└ SwordMaster: I played a lot of soccer when I was in the army. It’s strange seeing it here.","└ Heavenly Demon: Why would one play soccer in the military? This one cannot understand.","└ SwordMaster: I don’t know either. We just did. Even if it wasn’t soccer, we’d play with anything as long as we had a ball.","└ SwordMaster is right. Knights and soldiers alike will happily play as long as you give them a ball, lmao.","└ Military fact: The older they are, the more insanely good they are at foot volleyball, lmao.","└ In the army, the guys who are good at soccer and foot volleyball are kings;;","└ Suspiciously): Don’t you guys play rugby or American football? We do.","└ They probably play rugby too. But that comes down to preference.","└ And you have to wear armor to play American football;;","└ Just assume they play every ball sport imaginable with vacation days on the line.","└ No one can resist the promise of leave, lmao.","└ Cheonggu Princess: They’re having so much fun! As expected of Chae-U’s future mascot!","└ Who decided he was your mascot?","└ Cheonggu Princess: (Photo of Wonmo wearing a uniform) Can you really say that after seeing this?","└ Lmaoooo, she had that saved.","└ Honestly, he is ridiculously cute, lmao.","└ Put a uniform on Tyranno too.","└ Absolutely not. Tyranno must remain untouched.","└ Aren’t there already teams that use dragons as their symbol?","└ Quite a few countries and territories use dragons as their emblems;;","└ You might get hit with a massive lawsuit if you’re not careful, lmaooo.","└ But can anyone even sue Grylls?","└ No. But Chae-U might get caught in the crossfire, lmaooo.","└ King Leor: Don’t put something filthy on a sacred dragon;; Put our uniform on him instead.","└ Cheonggu Princess: You want him to wear that smelly chicken-head uniform? How horrifying!","└ King Leor: It’s a hawk, not a chicken; are your eyes broken?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I think it’s Coach Leor whose eyes are broken!","└ King Leor: Ffs—","└ Lmaoooooooo.","...!","└ Cheonggu Princess has been roasting King Leor nonstop lately, lmaooo.","└ Understandable. Cheonggu has climbed all the way up to fifth place in the rankings, lmao.","└ PraiseTheSun: Why am I the only one without a dragon? Why am I the only one without a dragon? Why am I the only one without a dragon? Why am I the only one without a dragon?","└ Not having a dragon is normal;","└ He talks like everyone else has one, lmaooo.","└ If every Tom, Dick, and Harry raised a hatchling, the world would’ve ended by now, lmao.","└ I’d rather raise Wonmo than Tyranno.","└ Same. Honestly, I’d choose the gentle-looking Wonmo over the prickly-looking Tyranno, lmao.","└ \"Gentle\": Eats his owner when he gets hungry.","└ Buuurp, lol.","As expected, the response was explosive.","Just reading the comments filled me with satisfaction.","I looked away from the gallery and turned toward Wonmo and Tyranno.","\"Kyuaaaaaak!!!\"","\"Piaaaaaaa!!\"","In the brief moment I had looked away, the two had started fighting.","They were tangled together, rolling around like a ball.","The instant I saw them, I jumped in and barely managed to pull them apart.",".","\"Why are you fighting?! Friends aren’t supposed to fight!\"","\"Kyu! Kyukyukyukyu! Kyukyu!\"","\"Pii! Pipipi! Piiiii!\"","I couldn’t understand a single word.","Judging by how worked up they both were, they must have been furious.","In the end, I summoned Kkobong, our resident animal-language interpreter, and asked her to translate.","First, I heard Wonmo’s side of the story.","\"It was his turn to score. But Tyranno stole the ball.\"","\"And Tyranno?\"","\"If something is taken, it belongs to whoever took it. That is only natural.\"","\"Hmm.\"","So it was because I had explained the rules too vaguely.","After learning what had happened, I carefully admonished them both.","I told them it was my fault for not explaining the rules clearly.","And that if they had a disagreement in the future, they should come to me first.","\"But! Pecking with your beak and biting with your teeth are unacceptable. Neither of you gets any snacks today.\"","\"Kyuuu?!\"","\"Piiiik?!\"","Wonmo and Tyranno both looked utterly horrified when they heard there would be no snacks.","But sometimes a little shock therapy was necessary.","If I spoiled them too much, they might grow up headed in the wrong direction.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"Oh. You’re here?\"","Wonmo and Tyranno were sitting side by side, dejected, when Father Raccoon came to visit me for the first time in a while.","As far as I knew, he had also been busy preparing for winter.","\"What did you find this time?\"","\"Keee...\"","Father Raccoon started to speak, only for his entire body to stiffen.","I had a pretty good idea what he had seen.","Tyranno.","Now that things had turned out this way, it might not be a bad idea to introduce Tyranno to the raccoon family.","\"Oh, right. Let me introduce you. This is Tyranno. As you can see, he’s a baby dragon—a hatchling.\"","\"K-Keeeng...?\"","Father Raccoon looked up at me with an expression that clearly said, A-A dragon?","I gently stroked his head to calm him down.","\"He won’t hurt you, so don’t worry. Didn’t you see the dragon that came here last time?\"","\"Keeeng...\"","\"So you did. That dragon left her baby with me. I don’t know why, though.\"","I finally managed to calm Father Raccoon.","He was still afraid, but his expression was considerably better than before.","Still, I would probably have to take things slowly before introducing Tyranno to his entire family. I still had plenty of other things to do.","At least Father Raccoon could give them a warning in advance.","’I hope the baby raccoons get along with the others.’","That was a matter for later.","For now, I checked what Father Raccoon had brought me.","It was an unusually large seed.","It looked like a coconut at first glance, but it was definitely a seed.","The thing was three times the size of my fist. I could probably grip it and use it as a blunt weapon.","\"What is this? A seed?\"","\"Keeeng!\"","Father Raccoon nodded with a bright smile.","I had no idea what kind of seed it was, but I figured I should plant it.","Father Raccoon had given it to me, so surely nothing strange would sprout from it.","I gave him a Fasting Pill as a reward and headed straight for the garden.","When I arrived, Ludwig was humming as he operated the threshing machine.","Kkobong was working beside him. I had bought her a farmer’s hat because I thought she might be bored, and it suited her surprisingly well.","\"Mister, I’m going to plant this.\"","\"#%%?\"","\"I don’t know what it is. Father Raccoon gave it to me.\"","The seed itself was much larger than my fist, so I would probably have to bury it deeper than usual.","I dug a hole with my shovel and placed the seed inside.","All I had to do was cover it with soil and pour water over it.","Now all that remained was to wait.","Ruuuumble—","\"Huh?\"","Not long after I planted the seed, faint tremors began running through the garden.","Ludwig and Kkobong stopped working and turned toward me.","Even the other animals looked this way.","\"...$%##$?\"","\"I-I don’t know. I just planted it...\"","Ludwig had asked what on earth I had planted, but I couldn’t give him an answer.","Then the garden slowly began to change.","A sprout emerged from the seed.","At first, it was tiny.","Whoooosh!","But the sprout gradually grew until its stalk became almost as thick as a tree trunk.","That alone was enough to tell me this was no ordinary plant.","The real problem, however, was its fruit.","A fruit slowly formed and continued swelling until it became as large as a house.","It was a vivid orange, with a slightly ridged and bumpy surface.","\"A pumpkin?\"","It was a pumpkin.","An absolutely gigantic pumpkin.","They said Cinderella rode to the castle in a pumpkin carriage.","If so, I imagined this was probably the pumpkin she had used.","But the Forest of Four Seasons was far removed from a \"fairy tale.\"","What did I mean by that?","Creeeak—","The center of the pumpkin slowly split open, revealing rows of razor-sharp teeth like those of a shark.","Then eyes and a nose appeared as well, making it look even more threatening.","\"Kyaaaaaaaa!!!\"","This wasn’t a fairy tale.","It was Halloween.","’What the hell did he give me...?’","I would think about that after I caught it."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204","paragraphs":["Jack-o’-Lantern (1)","The pumpkin monster known as the jack-o’-lantern could be considered the symbol of Halloween.","Its distinguishing features were its sharply carved mouth and the hollow openings that served as its eyes and nose.","And as the word \"lantern\" suggested, its interior was empty but filled with light.","From what I knew, jack-o’-lanterns rarely harmed people and generally limited themselves to playing pranks.","\"Kyaaaa! Kyaaaaaaa!\"","\"What the hell is this?\"","But that only applied when they were small.","The pumpkin head before me was as large as a house.","It looked threatening enough to swallow a person whole in a single bite.","The same went for its shriek. It sounded exactly like something a monster would make.","It certainly suited a fantasy world, but I was more worried than impressed.","’How am I supposed to kill something like this...?’","Unlike a beast, this thing was a plant. It had no obvious vital points.","There was fire, widely regarded as the natural enemy of all plants, but the question was whether it would work on this creature.","There was something else that bothered me as well.","’Father Raccoon wouldn’t have given me something dangerous...’","Until now, Father Raccoon had always brought me highly effective medicinal herbs or mushrooms.","That was why I had planted the seed he brought this time without much suspicion.","Yet the moment I planted it, some kind of pumpkin monster appeared.","I couldn’t help wondering whether it merely looked frightening and was actually friendly.","Thump!","Just as that thought crossed my mind, the jack-o’-lantern astonishingly launched itself high into the air.","I wondered how something that enormous could possibly jump so high, but I didn’t have long to think about it.","\"Fwooooop!\"","The jack-o’-lantern tilted its head backward.","\"Tutututututu!!!\"","Then it fired something from its mouth.","The projectiles were moving incredibly fast.","They weren’t too fast for me to dodge after seeing them, so I predicted their trajectories and evaded.","Papapapapak!","\"Kyuuu!\"","\"Piiiik!\"","The other animals hurriedly scattered as well.","I checked to see what the creature had spat out.","\"S-Seeds...?\"","The things fired by the jack-o’-lantern were none other than seeds.","They were enormous, comparable in size to the one I had planted.","But that wasn’t the end of it.","Rustle... Rustle...","The seeds began burrowing into the ground by themselves.","Horrified by the sight, I urgently shouted.","\"K-Kkobong! Pull those out, quickly! Hurry!\"","\"Understood!\"","\"Wonmo and Tyranno, you two help too! We’ll be in serious trouble if those things get underground!\"","\"Kyuuu!\"","\"Piiiii!\"","At my urgent command, my animal companions hurriedly removed the seeds as they burrowed into the soil.","Fortunately, the seeds sank into the ground rather slowly, so we barely managed to remove every last one.","Thud!","The jack-o’-lantern, however, remained perfectly fine.","Its massive body... Could I even call it a body?","Either way, the pumpkin came crashing back down.","Whoosh!","At that moment, Ludwig charged toward the jack-o’-lantern.","He was holding the Mithricon sword, though I had no idea when he had drawn it.","Apparently, he had been preparing to attack while the animals and I removed the seeds.","Shhhhh—","A green galaxy began flowing across the Mithricon sword in his hand.","At the same time, sharp aura formed around the entire weapon as if coating it.","Aura Blade.","It was a technique he had shown me several times before.","With the Mithricon sword and Aura Blade working together, it should be capable of cutting through steel with ease.","Shashashashak!","Ludwig appeared to swing his sword only once, yet dozens of slashes followed.","They were so fast that even my dynamic vision could barely track them.","He shouldn’t have been able to properly circulate the mana within his body, yet he could still move that quickly.","Just how strong had this man been outside the forest?","I grew more curious by the moment.","Thud! Thump!","Under Ludwig’s concise and efficient assault, the jack-o’-lantern was cleanly sliced into pieces.","It had been as large as a house, yet a few swings of his sword had killed it with absurd ease.","I was about to relax, thinking it was over.","Float—","The pumpkin fragments Ludwig had cut apart rose into the air.","Shhk! Shashak! Shak!","Then they began returning to their original positions.","Both Ludwig and I stared at them with our eyes wide open.","The moment all the pieces fused back together, the jack-o’-lantern’s distinctive expression reappeared on the pumpkin.","\"Kyaaaaaaa!!!\"","Ludwig retreated in bewilderment at the jack-o’-lantern’s shriek.","I was just as dumbfounded.","I had clearly seen inside it when Ludwig cut it to pieces.","’It was just an ordinary pumpkin.’","There had been nothing inside it other than a handful of seeds.","I hadn’t seen anything that could be called an inner core or nucleus.","Then how had the jack-o’-lantern regenerated?","Thump!","While I pondered the question, the jack-o’-lantern launched itself high into the air again.","Was it going to repeat the same attack?","I was about to raise my shield in preparation when—","Crack!","\"Fwooooop...! Gwehk!\"","Something struck the jack-o’-lantern as it tilted its head back, sending it plummeting to the ground.","I didn’t know what had hit it, but it had been shot down.","I turned my head, searching for the cause.","\"Ggueong.\"","It didn’t take me long to find it.","Largo had a brick clamped between his jaws.","Apparently, he had swung his long neck and hurled the brick like a catapult.","He was a literal living catapult.","Thanks to him, I had been spared quite a bit of trouble.","\"Thuuud!\"","The jack-o’-lantern crashed to the ground upside down.","We couldn’t afford to let this opportunity slip away.","Ludwig and I both rushed toward the fallen jack-o’-lantern without needing to say a word.","The creature was too busy trying to right itself.","It seemed to have difficulty controlling its body because of its enormous size.","Shashashashak! Shashashashashak!","Ludwig launched the first attack.","Just as before, the jack-o’-lantern was sliced into countless pieces.","Then it was my turn to finish it.","I enlarged my aura to an enormous size and brought it crashing down on the fragments.","Rather than trying to cut them, I struck with the intention of crushing them completely.","Booom! Bang! Bang!","The shattered chunks of pumpkin were reduced to pulp.","It was a waste, but there was nothing else I could do.","I had to deal with the immediate danger first.","And so, the jack-o’-lantern was not merely torn to pieces, but mashed into pulp.","At this point, surely it couldn’t regenerate again.","I muttered quietly.","\"...Did we get it?\"","\"You stupid bastard!\"","The moment I said that, Ludwig roared at me.","Startled by his sudden outburst, I turned toward him.","He was staring at me as if I had just uttered a forbidden phrase.","Only then did I realize what a terrible mistake I had made.","Float... Float...","And the consequences were catastrophic.","The jack-o’-lantern, which had been not only torn apart but mashed into pulp, was slowly regenerating.","Why the hell could it regenerate?","If it had been an animal, I might have understood.","There had been the case of the saber-toothed tiger—an individual whose regenerative abilities had been enhanced by possessing a heart comparable to a Dragon Heart.","But this creature wasn’t an animal. It was a plant.","Nor was there anywhere it could be absorbing nutrients from.","’Could it be the soil? No, that can’t be it. It doesn’t have any roots—’","The moment I remembered that the jack-o’-lantern had no \"roots,\" my mind snapped into focus.","It felt as though a bolt of lightning had flashed through my head.","I immediately turned around.","My gaze landed directly on the garden.","The garden where this creature had grown.","It was a theory that completely defied conventional wisdom, but this was a fantasy world.","More than that, this was the Forest of Four Seasons, a place where even the common sense of a fantasy world didn’t apply.","Rather than thinking logically, it might be better to follow my instincts.","\"Mister! Keep that bastard occupied!\"","\"Where are you going?\"","\"I just thought of something! And everyone, stay behind me just in case!\"","Immediately after giving the order, I picked up a shovel instead of my sword and shield.","I began digging in the part of the garden where I had planted the jack-o’-lantern.","And then—","\"Found it!\"","It didn’t take long for me to uncover the jack-o’-lantern’s \"roots.\"","I had no idea how it worked, but the roots were continuously supplying nutrients to the distant pumpkin.","’Does this world have Bluetooth roots too?’","At this rate, I wouldn’t be surprised if a Bluetooth showerhead appeared next.","Casting aside that useless thought, I grabbed the rhizome with all my strength.","Rustle!","Plants had wills of their own.","And this one was a monster.","The instant I seized its roots, vines burst out and frantically tried to bind my body.","One of them initially aimed for my neck, but I narrowly dodged it.","\"Hey! Kkobong! Grab this!\"","\"Uoh!\"","\"You guys grab one each too!\"","I gave instructions to Kkobong and the rest of my animal companions.","Once they had each seized a root or vine with their hands or mouths, I shouted with all my strength.","\"Puuuuull!\"","\"Kyuuuuuu!\"","\"Piiiiiiik!\"","I didn’t know whether the roots had burrowed extraordinarily deep or were simply resisting with all their might.","Even with one human and four animals pulling together, they showed no sign of coming free.","Behind us, Ludwig was keeping the giant pumpkin head at bay, but I had no idea how long he could hold out.","Rustle!","\"Kegh!\"","To make matters worse, one vine was still free.","Perhaps it had realized that I was the key figure, because it wrapped itself around my neck.","The pressure on my throat steadily increased, and my vision gradually began to blur.","But I refused to give up.","Through the roots in my hands, I could feel the other animals continuing to pull without surrendering.","If we failed to uproot this thing, there was no telling what else it might try.","Crack!","The fruits of our effort gradually began to show.","The distinctive sensation of roots being pulled free traveled through my hands.","I could vividly feel the creature struggling desperately to remain buried, but it was already too late.","The soil had already released its grip on the roots.","Even as the vine strangled me, I shouted.","\"Kegh! Now! Pull!\"","\"Uoooooh!!!\"","Crack-crack-crack-crack!","When we suddenly put more strength into it, the roots finally began emerging from the ground.","At the same time, the pressure around my neck grew even stronger.","But it was already too late.","Before long, the entire root system had been dragged out of the soil.","Craaaack! Pop!","We had finally uprooted the absurdly tenacious roots of the jack-o’-lantern.","They writhed as if they were alive, but the roots themselves were even more astonishing.","\"Kieeeeeee!\"","That wasn’t a root.","It was a miniature jack-o’-lantern.","And it was radiating a brilliant light.","Was it some kind of arrangement where the little one controlled the enormous one?","Whatever the case, we had found its weakness.","All that remained was to finish the job.","Thwack!","\"Kuehk!\"","When I punched the jack-o’-lantern hanging beneath the roots, it shrieked.","Apparently, it could feel pain.","It was similar to a fully grown mandrake.","That made things much easier.","I spoke to Kkobong.","\"Kkobong! Beat the crap out of this bastard!\"","\"Uoh!\"","Kkobong was far more proficient in martial arts than I was.","What did that mean?","Thudududududu!","\"Gguehk! Ggueeek! Ggueeeeeek!\"","It meant she pounded the creature like a punching bag.","As though venting all the stress that had accumulated until now, Kkobong gleefully pummeled it.","The more Kkobong struck it, the weaker the vine constricting my neck became.","The same was true of the giant pumpkin head Ludwig was fighting.","With its main body under attack, it could do nothing but twitch and was unable to move properly.","Limp—","After enduring a spectacular barrage of punches from Kkobong, the entire root system went limp.","The creature’s screams also died away.","It seemed to have lost consciousness.","When I looked at its face, its mouth, nose, and eyes had all vanished as though they had never existed.","Deciding that was enough, I was just about to tell Kkobong to stop when—","\"Bleurgh.\"","Something dropped out of the giant jack-o’-lantern’s mouth.","It was an orb radiating an orange glow.","Anyone could tell at a glance that it resembled an inner core.","However, it was rather large—about half the size of my fist.","If I tried swallowing it whole, it would get stuck in my throat.","\"The inner core is one thing, but I wonder if this is useful too.\"","I looked at the jack-o’-lantern’s main body.","I had no idea whether I could use it.","Now that it had expelled its inner core, it might have reverted to an ordinary pumpkin.","Even so, there was a high probability that it contained energy comparable to the inner core.","The fish had been the same.","Creatures that possessed inner cores were usually precious in their entirety.","\"#%@^?\"","Once the situation had settled down, Ludwig walked over and spoke to me.","He pointed somewhere, so I turned my head in that direction.","With the miniature main body incapacitated, the giant pumpkin head had become an ordinary pumpkin.","It was still just as enormous, though.","What could we possibly do with it?","\"We’ll eat it, I guess.\"","\"Eat it?\"","\"Yes.\"","Pumpkins had long been considered a winter delicacy.","\"Should we steam some pumpkin later?\"","Our food supply had just become even more abundant."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205","paragraphs":["Jack-o’-Lantern (2)","Setting aside Pumpkin Jack’s inner core and the other materials it had left behind, identifying exactly what this creature was took priority.","I had no idea what Father Raccoon had given me, but I needed to question him about it as well.","There was a lot to do.","First, I should consult Ludwig.","I asked him if he knew the creature’s identity.","\"Jack-o’-lantern\" was merely a name I had assigned to it based on my own knowledge. It was bound to have a proper name in this world.","\"Pumpkin Jack.\"","\"Pumpkin Jack?\"","That was the name he gave me.","I immediately understood its general meaning.","It was similar to \"jack-o’-lantern,\" yet different.","It was also remarkably straightforward.","Now that I knew its name, it would be best to ask the gallery for more details.","As luck would have it, I had taken several photos and videos.","So many unpredictable things kept happening that recording them had become a habit.","Title: What’s a Pumpkin Jack?","Wild Grylls","(A photo of Pumpkin Jack grinning wickedly)","(A video of Pumpkin Jack leaping into the air)","(A video of Pumpkin Jack regenerating)","(A photo of Pumpkin Jack’s inner core)","I planted a seed Father Raccoon brought me, and it suddenly turned into this thing;;","That pumpkin head kept regenerating no matter how many times we cut it apart, so we barely managed to find its roots and kill it.","It even spat out this strange inner core. Does anyone know what it is?","Ludwig says it’s called a Pumpkin Jack, but the name alone doesn’t tell me much.","└ Heavenly Demon: A monster with a face upon a pumpkin? Considering that faceless egg ghosts exist, perhaps it is not so strange.","└ Wild Grylls: Egg ghosts actually exist?","└ Heavenly Demon: They are commonly found in places overflowing with demonic energy.","└ Wild Grylls: So they’re similar to monsters.","└ They’re fundamentally different from monsters. Monsters existed that way from the beginning, while specters are humans who became corrupted.","└ A Cheonggui is also a specter created when someone is killed by a tiger. That’s why they lose their minds and start fighting whenever they see one.","└ Aren’t specters generally a level above monsters?","└ Usually. In the Central Plains, more people die fighting one another than fighting monsters.","└ What are you talking about? Lmao. They’d all die in front of a dragon anyway.","└ Dragons get killed by humans too, so obviously some specters can be stronger;;","└ SwordMaster: Pumpkin Jacks are extremely rare monsters, so this is fascinating. They’re supposed to appear only during a certain season and only at night.","└ Wild Grylls: Only at night? It openly fought me in broad daylight.","└ SwordMaster: That’s exactly why it’s fascinating. Though it’s possible that what I know is wrong.","└ Starlight Princess: Perhaps they’re simply easier to find at night. They emit light, after all.","└ Wild Grylls: It emitted light, but it also fired seeds like arrows.","└ Starlight Princess: I don’t know about that. They’re so rare that very little is known about them.","└ All-Father: There is a day known as the Day of the Dead. Pumpkin Jacks tend to appear frequently on that day.","└ Wild Grylls: That sounds ominous just from the name.","└ All-Father: It is a day when undead monsters appear with unusual frequency. Vengeful spirits, dullahans, ghouls, zombies, liches, and many others emerge in great numbers.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: That’s the busiest day of the year for priests! I participated in the fighting once, a long time ago!","└ What did you kill?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: A Death Knight!","└ Damn;; You killed a seriously tough one.","└ Aren’t Death Knights roughly as powerful as high-ranking knights?","└ Undead monsters are hard-countered by divine power, so they’re surprisingly easy for priests to kill.","└ PraiseTheSun: What are you going to do with that inner core? It looks too large to eat comfortably.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll store it for now. If nothing else works, I can ask Starlight Princess for help.","└ PraiseTheSun: Really? Then what about the pumpkin? Are you planning to eat that enormous thing by yourself?","└ GrowBigAndStrong: For reference, pumpkins are harvested in autumn and become incredibly delicious if you let them mature through winter.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s what they say.","└ PraiseTheSun: Then give me a little when the time comes, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: Me too, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Sure, I’ll give some to all of you.","└ You mean you’ll put it up in the auction house, right? Lmao.","└ My mouth is already watering, lmao.","I had never said anything about putting it up in the auction house.","In any case, it was clearly a rare monster.","I had no idea how Father Raccoon had managed to find it.","Once I finished checking the comments, I called Father Raccoon over.","There was no way he had brought it to play a prank on me, so why had he given it to me?","\"Keeeng! Keeeeng! Keng!\"","\"He says he didn’t know either. The seed smelled good, so he thought it would be good to eat.\"","\"Hmm.\"","According to Father Raccoon, he hadn’t expected me to plant the seed.","Animals ate seeds if they looked tasty, whereas humans planted those seeds in the ground.","On top of that, Father Raccoon had probably only seen my garden recently.","This whole incident had resulted from a difference in how we thought.","’Still, the outcome wasn’t bad.’","I had obtained Pumpkin Jack’s inner core and an enormous supply of food.","I was somewhat worried that insects or other beasts might eat the giant pumpkin.","I could deal with insects using repellent, but there wasn’t much I could do about beasts other than fight them.","Knock, knock—","’At least it’s tough.’","The one consolation was that the pumpkin’s rind was extremely hard.","Ordinary teeth wouldn’t even leave a mark on it.","’I’ll use the pumpkin growing from the roots for lunch.’","Pumpkins weren’t root vegetables.","Strangely enough, however, the main body hanging from the roots was itself a pumpkin.","It was the creature Kkobong had beaten unconscious.","All of its vines had now been removed, leaving only the main body behind.","It was small compared to the giant pumpkin, but still large enough to feed all of us.","There was also a chance it might wake up again, so I needed to deal with it quickly.","’I’ll steam this one.’","Lunchtime was approaching, and I had worked up an appetite after exerting myself for the first time in a while.","But before I began preparing lunch, there was one more thing I needed to do.","\"Yes, right there. Stack them like that.\"","\"Here?\"","\"That’s right. Think of it as arranging them symmetrically.\"","We were building another oven.","Now that there were more mouths to feed, productivity had become important.","Preparing the ingredients didn’t take very long, but cooking them did.","If I built another oven, I could reduce the overall cooking time.","’Since we’re doing it anyway, let’s make this one bigger.’","I made it larger than the previous oven, just in case.","Naturally, I received help from Passing Dwarf with the iron plates.","When I promised to give him some pumpkin to have with his drinks later, he gladly provided them.","With Ludwig’s help, we finished the oven quickly and immediately began preparing our meal.","’Let’s see. To make steamed pumpkin...’","It would have been much easier if I had a steamer, but unfortunately, I didn’t.","Still, steaming something wasn’t difficult.","All I had to do was pour water into the bottom of a pot and suspend the pumpkin above it.","Keeping it out of the water was simple as well. Placing a small bowl inside the pot would suffice.","Since pumpkin was naturally sweet, I planned to serve it as dessert.","\"All right. Let’s eat.\"","\"Kyuuu~\"","\"Piii! Pii!\"","Around halfway through the meal, I began steaming the pumpkin.","At this rate, it should be ready just as we finished eating.","Sure enough, once everyone had finished their meal, I took out the steamed pumpkin.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","\"Oh...\"","It had definitely been orange when I removed the seeds.","But after being steamed, it glittered with a golden color.","It looked as though it had been coated in honey, even though I hadn’t put any on it.","The steamed pumpkin looked unmistakably sweet.","Everyone was practically drooling at the sight.","\"Slurp... No. It’s hot. You have to wait.\"","\"Kyuuu...\"","\"Piiiii...\"","The little ones stared at me longingly after I stopped them.","Their silent protest seemed to say, Hurry up and put that steamed pumpkin in my mouth!","But I was the cook.","Before serving it to the others, I had to taste it myself.","It had only just finished steaming, so wisps of steam rose from it.","Munch, munch—","\"Kiyaaa!\"","An exclamation of delight escaped me the moment I took a spoonful.","Was this pumpkin or honey?","The phrase \"honey-sweet pumpkin\" suited it perfectly.","After seeing my reaction, the little ones grew even more restless.","Wonmo, whose appetite was especially powerful, began frantically scratching my knee with his forepaws.","\"...All right, all right. Here you go.\"","\"Kyuaaaa!\"","\"Piiiiii!\"","I distributed the steamed pumpkin among them.","Everyone received an equal portion.","\"Kyuaa! Kyua!\"","\"Piiak! Piiaak!\"","\"Hot! Hot!\"","Oh, right.","I had forgotten to tell them to eat slowly because it was hot.","Once they adjusted to the heat, however, they ate it happily.","The same was true of Ludwig.","He gave me a thumbs-up instead of voicing his opinion.","Lastly, Fast Sloth ate leisurely with his usual slow movements.","What was interesting was that his hands were moving faster than normal.","To anyone else, he would still have looked painfully slow, but I could tell he was moving much faster than usual.","’Good.’","Wonmo went into the cave for a nap, and Tyranno followed him, apparently planning to sleep as well.","The rest of us finished cleaning up.","Pumpkin Jack had made an enormous mess, after all.","After tidying everything, I took the inner core out of my pocket.","It was a fairly large inner core that continued to emit an orange glow.","’Should I just eat it?’","I had consumed many inner cores by now.","Thanks to them, my aura grew larger by the day.","As a bonus, Ludwig looked increasingly troubled whenever he saw it.","What would happen if I ate this one too?","It would be difficult to swallow, but it seemed worth trying.","\"Should I try eating this?\"","\"...\"","Nod—","When I asked Ludwig for advice, he unexpectedly indicated that it should be fine.","I already fought by relying on my overwhelming physical capacity, so there was no harm in increasing it further.","I could think about forming an Aura Blade later.","For now, I should continue increasing my raw capacity.","With even Ludwig giving his approval, there was no longer any reason to hesitate.","’It bothers me that it’s large enough to be difficult to swallow...’","Still, I would have to force it down.","Breaking it apart would make the core easier to swallow, but it would also reduce its effectiveness by half.","I nodded and immediately assumed a cross-legged meditation posture.","When Ludwig saw me sit down, he silently picked up his sword.","It appeared he intended to guard me in case something invaded the shelter.","’He really is dependable.’","I smiled briefly, then exhaled slowly and placed the inner core in my mouth.","I strained my throat as much as possible and forced myself to swallow it.","The sensation of a massive sphere traveling down my esophagus was far from pleasant.","Still, it somehow reached my stomach, allowing me to relax.","’The energy of the heavens...’","The instant I swallowed the inner core, I began reciting the mnemonic formula the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","I remembered every word of it perfectly.","Each verse was long, but that wasn’t a problem.","Thump! Thump! Thump!","The energy within the core gradually began spreading throughout my body.","Pumpkin Jack’s inner core contained far more energy than the fish’s core had.","No matter how much energy I absorbed, it never seemed to diminish.","Thanks to that, my dantian was soon filled to the brim with internal energy.","At this rate, I wondered if it might burst.","’Just in case, I should circulate it faster...’","Growing anxious, I pushed the cultivation technique even harder.","If not for the mnemonic formula the Heavenly Demon had taught me, this might have become quite dangerous.","Eventually, I absorbed the entire inner core and slowly opened my eyes.","When I did, I had the illusion that the world had become much brighter than before.","\"Hmm.\"","Realizing I was awake, Ludwig relaxed his vigilant stance.","I bowed my head to express my gratitude.","Then I looked around the cave and noticed that the little ones were gone.","Instead, I could hear them playing outside.","When I stepped out, the sun was already setting.","The days had grown shorter with winter approaching, but absorbing the inner core had also taken quite a long time.","’I don’t feel particularly different.’","Other than having far more mana within my body, I couldn’t identify any notable changes.","Still, increasing my raw capacity was undoubtedly a good thing.","Delighted, I made a post in the gallery.","Most people congratulated me, while the anonymous users responded with jealousy.","└ Aren’t you eventually going to explode with a bang?","└ Hasn’t that happened to someone before?","└ There was someone whose mana reserves were so abnormally large that cracks formed throughout their entire body.","└ Heavenly Demon: That once happened to this lady. However, thanks to your aid, I was able to survive.","So they said, anyway.","Night had arrived, so I began preparing dinner.","And then...","\"What is this now?\"","\"Kyuuuuu! Kyukyu!\"","\"Piiiiik!\"","It was only after nightfall that I discovered the effect of Pumpkin Jack’s inner core.","I could see as clearly as if it were morning.","The problem lay with my eyes and mouth.","Powerful beams of light were shining in whichever direction I looked.","Turning my head made no difference.","The light followed my gaze perfectly.","\"Now I’ve become a human lantern?\"","Light was pouring from my eyes and mouth.","Extremely bright light, at that.","I had become a human lantern.","Being able to shoot light from my eyes meant this was basically—","\"LASER BEEEEAM!!!\"","\"Kyuuuuuuu!!\"","\"Piiiii! Piiiiii!\"","It looked freaking stupid, but it was fun.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206","paragraphs":["Jack-o’-Lantern (3)","Light was coming from my eyes.","Usually, that expression was used figuratively.","It didn’t mean that someone’s eyes were literally emitting light. It simply meant they had shown keen interest in something.","But actual light was shining from my eyes.","Thanks to everyone’s reactions, I noticed it fairly quickly.","Wonmo and Tyranno loved seeing light come out of my eyes.","Ludwig, on the other hand... reacted as though he had witnessed something utterly bizarre.","He stared at me with an expression that seemed to ask, Is this thing truly human?","He must have spent many years as a paladin, but I was probably the first case like this he had ever encountered.","Title: Who Has Light Coming from His Eyes, Nose, and Mouth?","Wild Grylls","(A photo of Grylls’s face glowing from the eyes, nose, and mouth inside the dark cave)","Me!","└ Heavenly Demon: What in the world happened to you? Have you been possessed by an evil spirit?","└ Wild Grylls: No. This happened after I ate Pumpkin Jack’s inner core.","└ Heavenly Demon: Does that inner core ordinarily possess such an effect?","└ SwordMaster: I’ve never even heard of a Pumpkin Jack possessing an inner core.","└ Everything he encounters has an inner core;","└ Even an ordinary fish had one, so whatever, lol.","└ At this point, we should assume that every living creature has one.","└ But judging by the picture alone, he looks like a freaking ghost, lmaooo.","└ Is he actually human?","└ Lmaoooooooo.","└ Why is such a simple question so funny? Lmaooo.","└ It’s a genuinely fundamental question, lmao.","└ The more I see of him, the more he seems to be turning into something inhuman, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: Do you feel any urges to eat human flesh or drink blood?","└ Wild Grylls: Why would you say something so terrifying?;;","└ Starlight Princess: It appears in some records of people transforming into specters. There’s an old account that mentions such urges. Fortunately, it doesn’t seem as though you’re becoming one.","└ Wild Grylls: ;;;","└ Starlight Princess: Still, you should remain cautious. There are no records of people emitting light from their eyes, even in ancient texts.","└ All-Father: There was one such person. A man whose eyes had been gouged out used glowing objects as prosthetic eyes.","└ Starlight Princess: Someone actually did that? Why?","└ All-Father: The records offer no explanation beyond, \"Because it looked impressive.\"","└ Honestly, it does sound cool, lmao.","└ How could anyone resist having glowing eyes? Lmaooo.","└ Passing Dwarf: Does the light keep shining if you cut off your head? Because then you’d be a real human lantern.","└ Wild Grylls: Don’t say something so horrifying;;","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: What did Sir Ludwig say about it?!","└ Wild Grylls: Other than looking at me as if he’d seen something completely bizarre, he seems fine. He also told me to turn my head because it was too bright.","└ So you’re just being a nuisance, lmaooo.","└ Will you even be able to sleep? Lmao.","└ Cheonggu Princess: We demons have inverted eyes, while Mr. Grylls has luminous eyes! Are you perhaps one of the Celestials?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t know anything about that;; And what are the Celestials? Is that an actual race?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I was just saying it for fun!","└ They do exist. Though they’re called angels, not Celestials.","└ Aren’t angels demigod-level beings?","└ Yeah. That’s why most people who ascend to the heavens or attain immortality become angels.","└ Oh. Then did the Blood Demon become an angel too?","└ How would I know? Lmao. It’s only mythology.","└ Angel Blood Demon, let’s go.","└ That combination does not work at all, lmao.","└ Meanwhile, you can’t even see Grylls’s face.","└ The cave is dark. It can’t be helped.","The gallery erupted into an uproar after I made the post.","Had any of them ever seen someone like me before?","Probably not.","I closed the gallery and looked outside the cave.","Like a high-performance flashlight, the beam brightly illuminated the darkness.","With this, I should have no difficulty navigating at night.","’But how do I turn it off?’","The question was whether I could control it.","I tried several things, such as straining my eyes and blinking repeatedly, but the light stubbornly refused to go out.","There was no noticeable change in the mana inside my body either.","It was the same as before.","Was this some kind of passive ability, or could I control it at will?","’It’ll be awkward if I can’t control it.’","I turned toward Ludwig.","He immediately frowned and squinted.","Not being able to look anyone in the face was a serious drawback.","The little ones enjoyed it, but even their fascination would fade before long.","’Let’s try circulating my cultivation technique first. Since this came from an inner core, there must be something inside me.’","I began circulating the cultivation technique to see if I could sense anything unusual.","’There’s nothing in particular.’","Other than the cold energy, I felt nothing unusual within my dantian.","Was it truly a passive ability?","The light hadn’t appeared before sunset, so that seemed highly likely.","Still, I couldn’t give up.","If I couldn’t control it at will, the ability would become far less useful.","I began conducting all kinds of experiments with help from Ludwig and the gallery.","└ Can’t you smack the back of your head to turn it off and on? That works when a lantern breaks.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s for when it won’t turn on, you lunatic.","They weren’t particularly helpful.","It was a phenomenon none of them had ever seen before, so everyone seemed equally lost.","In the end, I decided to leave the matter for tomorrow.","As long as I closed my eyes and kept my mouth shut, it was fine.","I couldn’t do anything about the light coming from my nose, but that much was bearable.","’Still, I really do seem to be turning into something other than human.’","My absurdly expanding aura and the cold energy within me still fell within the bounds of common sense.","They were rare, but not entirely unprecedented.","Yet according to the gallery, there wasn’t even a single mention in the literature of anyone emitting light from their eyes, nose, and mouth.","Starlight Princess said similar symptoms had been observed in some people transforming into specters, but even she wasn’t certain.","’Aren’t inner cores always supposed to be beneficial?’","It would have been nice to know about this effect beforehand.","Unlike the protagonists of certain novels, I had no status window or system.","I had no choice but to investigate every new ability myself, one by one.","At least the amount of mana in my body had increased tremendously.","I closed my eyes and considered what I needed to do tomorrow.","’Winter will arrive soon. Five days at the latest.’","The steadily falling temperature was proof.","After several bouts of rain, the weather had suddenly grown much colder.","It was about time I obtained winter clothing for Ludwig as well.","Passing Dwarf should be able to help with that.","’First, I need to do some logging. It might snow soon, so I should also keep the fire burning strongly.’","Once I finished all those tasks, I planned to visit the Orichalcum Cave.","Now that light came from my eyes, I ought to test its performance.","The cave where I lived was too small, and the campfire made it difficult to tell how effective the light truly was.","’We’re only going there and coming straight back. I can introduce Ludwig to the place while we’re at it.’","Our winter preparations were nearly complete.","We wouldn’t need to venture far from the shelter for a while.","The only remaining task was perhaps creating an emergency exit, but that wouldn’t take long.","I slowly drifted off to sleep while planning the following day.","***","Morning arrived.","The weather was slightly warmer than it had been the day before.","\"The light stopped coming from my eyes once the sun came up.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Apparently, it was a passive ability that activated only at night or in dark places.","Wonmo and Tyranno were naturally disappointed when they discovered this.","I stroked their heads and began preparing breakfast.","First, I needed to head upstream and retrieve the fish trap.","\"Hm?\"","The moment I reached the river, something felt strange.","The river was usually so clear that I could see everything inside it.","However, most creatures were difficult to distinguish because they moved quickly and were naturally camouflaged.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","But now things were slightly different.","Points of light glittered throughout the river.","They traveled along the current before getting caught in the fish trap with a thump.","The area around the trap glittered like a mass of gold, immediately drawing my attention.","’W-What is that?’","I didn’t know, so I decided to retrieve the trap first.","Kkobong, who had accompanied me, helped as well.","Once we hauled it out, I saw several fish flopping around inside.","Their bellies—the parts containing their inner cores—were glowing particularly brightly.","Could it be?","I immediately gathered everything and returned to the shelter.","There was no reason to delay.","When I extracted the inner core from one of the fish, I confirmed my suspicion.","Although the glow was extremely faint, the inner core twinkled like a star.","It seemed to be another effect of the Pumpkin Jack’s inner core.","’Come to think of it, my subspace backpack and the bottle containing the inner cores are glowing too.’","I had only just noticed them.","Perhaps the effect hadn’t fully developed yesterday because I had only recently consumed the core.","This would be enormously useful.","It should make finding medicinal herbs much easier.","Since I wasn’t an expert, asking the gallery about each and every plant had been exhausting.","’Still, I should probably ask the gallery how this ability works.’","I gave Ludwig a rough explanation.","After hearing it, he looked mildly surprised, as though he had never heard of such a thing.","At this point, another question occurred to me.","What about the mithril that had been judged to be alive?","Would it glitter like gold dust too?","Curious, I headed toward the back of the cave.","Flash! Flash!","The mithril wasn’t merely glowing.","It was flashing so brightly that it hurt my eyes.","The light came from deep within the cave, and something about it made me even more reluctant to approach.","I had a feeling that trying to mine it would only bring me trouble.","It felt even more unsettling now.","’Still, it can’t hurt me if I leave it alone...’","The discovery left a bitter taste in my mouth, but it seemed I would need to regularly explore the area around the cave from now on.","There was a limit to how many Fasting Pills I could make using only the medicinal herbs Father Raccoon brought me.","For now, I decided to explore alone and test the ability.","I didn’t forget to bring Fast Sloth with me, just in case.","’That thing is glowing almost as brightly as the mithril.’","It was the sapling Let’sGrowTrees had given me.","All the other plants grew quickly, but that one alone continued to develop at a slow pace.","Had they truly given me a World Tree sapling?","It was becoming increasingly difficult not to suspect it.","’I heard fully grown World Trees are larger than most villages. Does it even have enough space to grow?’","If it reached that size, it would destroy the entire shelter.","I dismissed the useless thought and explored the area around the cave.","Surprisingly, it was difficult to find anything that glowed.","That was probably because most of the vegetation consisted of ordinary weeds.","’What exactly determines whether something glows? Does it have to be at least as valuable as an inner core?’","There was a lot to consider.","After briefly looking around, I returned to the cave.","Once I got back, I finished preparing for our journey to the Orichalcum Cave.","I intended to determine whether the light from my eyes was a passive or active ability.","Naturally, everyone would be coming with us.","Leaving only a few behind might be more dangerous than taking the entire group.","’Even if someone raids the shelter, the only thing they can steal is food.’","And so, everyone at the shelter set out for the Orichalcum Cave.","Ludwig rode on Largo and quietly followed behind me.","’I should install a saddle for him later.’","If he was going to ride a giraffe like a horse, a saddle was essential.","Even while heading toward the cave, I gathered every glowing medicinal herb I encountered.","Then, partway through the journey, I spotted something shining underground.","Could it be an expensive mineral?","Without delay, I took out my shovel and pickaxe.","\"Mr. Ludwig, there’s something down here. Let’s start digging.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Following my instructions, Ludwig began shoveling diligently.","I broke apart the hard ground with the pickaxe, while Ludwig scooped away the loose soil with his shovel.","After repeating the process, we gradually approached the glowing object.","Ruuuuumble!","Without warning, the entire ground began to shake.","Ludwig and I immediately stopped working.","Judging from everything I had experienced until now, earthquakes were rarely a good sign.","And sure enough—","RUMBLE! RUMBLE! RUMBLE!","Something began surging out of the ground.","We hurriedly retreated from the rapidly rising earth.","At last, the majestic figure revealed itself.","\"A-A Guardian...?\"","It was a Guardian—a golem made entirely of earth.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","The core embedded in the Guardian’s chest was shining brilliantly.","\"#%%#$?\"","Ludwig asked what the hell I had done.","I couldn’t give him an answer."]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207","paragraphs":["There’s Space Behind the Pillar (1)","Fortunately, we didn’t end up having to fight a fierce battle against the guardian.","Just as different materials possessed different properties, the guardians also seemed to have different personalities.","While the orichalcum guardian had reacted aggressively to mana, the earth guardian showed no particular reaction.","It simply rose from the ground, stared intently at us, and then moved elsewhere. That was the end of it.","\"Phew.\"","I breathed a sigh of relief as I watched the earth guardian leave.","In terms of fighting strength, our side actually had a considerable advantage.","Ludwig went without saying, and I had experience fighting a guardian as well.","Still, there was no reason to waste our strength, and a battle might inadvertently provoke the other beings in the surrounding area.","Besides, despite the fact that we had disturbed it first, it had simply left without making a fuss. It seemed to have a fairly mild temperament.","\"...Let’s get going.\"","\"Mm.\"","With the situation resolved, we resumed our journey.","This incident taught me not to touch anything shiny carelessly.","Especially if it was buried in the ground.","I headed toward the orichalcum cave, gathering medicinal herbs along the way.","A few beasts appeared as we advanced, but they immediately fled.","’We have a much larger group, after all.’","It had long been said that there was strength in numbers.","Moreover, most of our group members were quite formidable, so the beasts probably didn’t even want to approach us.","\"Kyuooo! Kyu! Kyu!\"","\"Screeech!\"","\"Oh, come on, you two.\"","Except for the two weakest members of the group, of course.","I barely managed to break up the fight between the two over a rabbit they had just caught.","From the looks of things, they had caught the rabbit as it was fleeing, but there would be no end to it if they fought like this every time.","\"If you fight again, neither of you gets a snack. Got it?\"","\"Kyuooo...\"","\"Piiing...\"","After making them reconcile, we resumed our journey toward the orichalcum cave.","Perhaps it was because we had applied insect repellent, or perhaps because winter was approaching, but we weren’t troubled by insects.","’Come to think of it, wasn’t this the chickens’ territory?’","I glanced around. If I remembered correctly, this place belonged to the black chickens.","They were almost as tall as Largo.","I remembered Wonmo encountering them during his strange little adventure, leading to all sorts of trouble.","’There aren’t any signs of them. Did something happen?’","\"Kyuoo.\"","\"$%’#?\"","Or perhaps they were simply preparing for the approaching winter.","In that case, I figured there was no need to go looking for them.","—Cock-a-doodle-doo!!!","Just then, a rooster’s crow echoed throughout the entire forest, as though warning us not to come any closer.","It seemed they had an uncanny ability to detect intruders entering their territory.","\"Kyuoo!!!\"","Upon hearing the cry, Wonmo came scurrying over to me.","He clung tightly to my leg, apparently still terrified by what had happened back then.","Well, he had been surrounded by chicks much larger than himself, so his reaction was understandable.","I probably would’ve pissed myself too if I’d been surrounded by chickens.","\"It’s okay. It’s okay. There’s no one around.\"","\"Kyuoo...\"","Seeing Wonmo whimper, Ludwig tilted his head and asked me a question.","He must have realized that something had happened here after seeing Wonmo react to the rooster’s crow.","\"Yes. Wonmo had a rough time with the chicks.\"","\"Chi... cks?\"","\"You know, the little ones that go cheep, cheep.\"","When I imitated the sound of chicks chirping, Ludwig seemed to understand and nodded.","I continued onward while patting the trembling Wonmo on the back.","Tyranno watched us with a strange expression, but I ignored him.","\"This is the place.\"","\"Hmm.\"","After some time, we arrived at the orichalcum cave.","Ludwig carefully examined the cave entrance, which appeared perfectly ordinary from the outside.","Meanwhile, I took out the Light crystal orb I had received from King Leor.","Light might come from my eyes, but there was still nothing better than this for exploring a cave.","Besides, there was no guarantee that light would shine from my eyes every time I entered a dark place.","Maybe it only happened at night rather than simply in darkness. I needed to test it.","Flash!","After I tapped the Light crystal orb a few times, it began emitting light.","The crystal orb then floated gently into the air.","I could faintly hear Ludwig exclaim in admiration behind me.","King Leor had previously told me that it was quite an expensive item.","\"All right. Let’s go.\"","\"Mm.\"","\"We’re leaving Largo here, right?\"","We left Largo outside the cave due to his size.","One might wonder whether he would run away, but Ludwig didn’t seem concerned about that.","Still, just to be safe, I should have a set of reins made for him later. The dwarf would probably make them for me.","Now that all our preparations were complete, I entered the cave with the crystal orb floating above me.","Flash!","\"Kyuoo! Kyuoo!\"","\"Screeech!\"","The moment I set foot inside the pitch-dark cave, light burst from my eyes.","The beams moved wherever I looked. It was truly bizarre.","At least my eyes didn’t hurt. That was some consolation.","If they had hurt, I would have done everything in my power to learn how to control it.","’There might be animals that are sensitive to light.’","Caves were naturally extremely dark.","Consequently, many cave-dwelling animals either had poor eyesight or eyes that had completely degenerated.","Well, this was a fantasy world, so there might also be animals whose vision had developed to an extraordinary degree.","Besides, there was no guarantee that light would shine from my eyes every time I entered a dark place.","Maybe it only happened at night rather than simply in darkness. I needed to test it.","Flash!","After I tapped the Light crystal orb a few times, it began emitting light.","The crystal orb then floated gently into the air.","I could faintly hear Ludwig exclaim in admiration behind me.","King Leor had previously told me that it was quite an expensive item.","\"All right. Let’s go.\"","\"Mm.\"","\"We’re leaving Largo here, right?\"","We left Largo outside the cave due to his size.","One might wonder whether he would run away, but Ludwig didn’t seem concerned about that.","Still, just to be safe, I should have a set of reins made for him later. The dwarf would probably make them for me.","Now that all our preparations were complete, I entered the cave with the crystal orb floating above me.","Flash!","\"Kyuoo! Kyuoo!\"","\"Screeech!\"","The moment I set foot inside the pitch-dark cave, light burst from my eyes.","The beams moved wherever I looked. It was truly bizarre.","At least my eyes didn’t hurt. That was some consolation.","If they had hurt, I would have done everything in my power to learn how to control it.","’There might be animals that are sensitive to light.’","Caves were naturally extremely dark.","Consequently, many cave-dwelling animals either had poor eyesight or eyes that had completely degenerated.","Well, this was a fantasy world, so there might also be animals whose vision had developed to an extraordinary degree.","Even so, that wouldn’t change the fact that they would be sensitive to light.","\"Let’s head down this way.\"","The rope I had installed previously was still there.","It wasn’t a sheer descent, and there were places to plant one’s feet along the way.","I had only installed the rope because the slope could be dangerous.","\"Kyuoo. Kyu.\"","\"Pii. Pii.\"","True to their small size, Wonmo and Tyranno hopped their way down.","Ludwig, Kkobong, and I slowly descended while holding on to the rope.","If any of us slipped here, there was a good chance we would be seriously injured.","\"Heave-ho.\"","It had been a long time since I last visited the orichalcum cave.","It was still as dark and gloomy as ever.","The guardian had already been defeated, but just in case, we planned to avoid using mana as much as possible.","\"$%$...\"","\"This is all orichalcum. Take a look.\"","I gave Ludwig a brief explanation as he took in the orichalcum cave for the first time.","The entire cave was made of orichalcum, and he was free to take some if he wanted.","However, he needed to be careful about using mana. There was no telling what might emerge.","\"Crunch! Crunch! Munch! Munch!\"","\"Kyuoo...\"","Just as he had happily eaten mithril last time, Tyranno began eating the orichalcum.","The highlight was Wonmo staring at him as though he couldn’t comprehend what he was seeing.","To Tyranno, it probably felt as though delicious snacks were scattered everywhere.","\"I don’t see anything glowing.\"","Orichalcum was sensitive to mana but contained almost no energy of its own.","It seemed that only orichalcum saturated with mana glittered like gold dust.","’We’ll just look around and leave... Hm?’","Sparkle! Sparkle!","Having completed my experiment, I had been about to leave when I noticed something glittering behind an orichalcum pillar.","It was even much larger than the core that had been buried underground.","It was shining that brightly despite being surrounded on all sides by mana-absorbing orichalcum?","There was a high probability that it contained a terrifying amount of mana.","’Hmm... Maybe we shouldn’t go over there.’","Curiosity killed the cat.","Considering the circumstances, approaching it would be dangerous.","Hadn’t we nearly landed ourselves in serious trouble just moments ago by disturbing a guardian?","Still, I couldn’t ignore the glimmer behind the pillar.","It would be best to gather everyone’s opinions first. I called out to Ludwig, who was examining a stone.","\"Mister, take a look over there for a moment.\"","\"Hmm?\"","\"There’s something over there. Should we go?\"","Perfect communication was still difficult, but he could understand me to some degree when I used hand gestures.","When I pointed in that direction, Ludwig turned his head toward it.","Once he realized that something was there, he paused to consider it.","I intended to decide whether to approach it after hearing his opinion.","\"@#.\"","Eventually, Ludwig nodded and spoke in a tone that suggested we should go.","When I asked whether it would be dangerous, he replied,","\"Know. Not know. Difference. Big.\"","There was a big difference between proceeding while aware of the danger and proceeding without knowing about it.","That seemed to be the gist of what he meant. His tone conveyed as much.","My eyes widened at how much Ludwig’s Korean had improved in such a short time.","Were most of the people and animals here simply gifted with languages?","When I asked him about that as well, he shrugged. Apparently, he didn’t know either.","’Could it be the influence of the Forest of Four Seasons?’","Perhaps those who were barely affected physically became more intelligent instead.","It was only a hypothesis, but it wasn’t entirely ridiculous.","After all, I was already evolving into a superhuman myself.","This might be something I needed to watch out for in the future. Once I had finished preparing, I moved forward.","’There’s a space behind this pillar...’","There really was.","It had been concealed so cleverly that I had never noticed it before.","I also hadn’t examined the place thoroughly since every surface around me was covered in orichalcum.","The orichalcum was so valuable that I hadn’t felt any need to explore farther, and its splendid appearance had captured all my attention.","’Just in case, I should have the others stay back.’","I took the lead with my sword and shield in hand, while Ludwig stood directly behind me.","Kkobong would protect Wonmo and Tyranno. This was the best formation.","We then rounded the dark pillar and slowly peered ahead.","The space behind it was surprisingly large. I had no idea a place like this existed.","\"...A chest?\"","\"...\"","There was even a lone chest sitting there.","Perhaps it was the object I had detected, because it glittered so brightly that it made my eyes ache slightly.","Why in the world was there a chest here?","Just as the question crossed my mind—","\"Mimic.\"","\"What?\"","\"Mimic.\"","Ludwig deduced the chest’s true identity in a slightly tense voice.","A mimic. It was a name I had heard before as well.","A monster that disguised itself as a treasure chest to deceive anyone who approached it.","Come to think of it, the very fact that a chest was sitting alone inside an orichalcum cave was suspicious.","\"What should we do?\"","\"Hmm...\"","Ludwig pondered my question.","Normally, we would have simply ignored it and moved on. However, this was a mimic.","If we killed it, it would surely drop treasure of tremendous value.","There was no telling what kind of treasure it might yield. It could be gold and jewels, or perhaps even a miraculous elixir.","I didn’t particularly need riches, but an elixir would be a different story.","’And that glow doesn’t look ordinary.’","Furthermore, an elixir seemed more likely than gold or jewels.","Ludwig seemed to know this as well, because he nodded gravely.","It was a signal that we should subjugate it. Understanding his intention, I asked him for advice.","\"Do you know how to kill a mimic?\"","Ludwig nodded at my question.","According to his rough explanation, mimics were generally extremely slow.","Since they were essentially nothing more than lumps of flesh, they apparently moved at a snail’s pace.","Their tongues, however, were unbelievably quick, and people often had their weapons snatched away by them.","Therefore, ranged attacks were essential. I, in particular, could launch ranged attacks using aura.","\"So you’re saying I should attack it with aura from a distance?\"","\"Correct.\"","\"Stay back for a moment.\"","Now that I knew the strategy, all that remained was to put it into action.","After telling Ludwig and my animal companions to back away, I circulated my mana.","Hummmmm!!!","A pillar of aura rose into the air. Perhaps thanks to Pumpkin Jack’s internal core, the pillar had grown even larger.","I wondered when I would finally be able to use an Aura Blade.","Setting that lament aside, I prodded the mimic like a fencer to provoke it.","To kill it efficiently, it would be better to tear up its insides than to smash the chest itself.","Tap, tap—tap—","\"Grrrrrr...\"","After I poked the chest several times, an ominous growl emerged from it.","So it really was a mimic.","In that case, I needed to provoke it further. I continued jabbing the mimic.","Perhaps it could no longer endure the irritation, because the mimic finally reacted.","Slaash! Whip!","First, long arms emerged from the slightly open lid.","Then—","Shwoooop!!!","Thick, elongated legs burst from underneath the chest.","Its form resembled the mushroom people I had seen a few weeks earlier.","As I stared speechlessly at the sight, a huge tongue slid out of the chest.","As an added bonus, its gaping opening was lined with razor-sharp teeth.","\"ROOOOOAAAR!!!\"","\"...\"","The creature sprayed filthy saliva everywhere as it roared.","The rest of the group was safely behind me, but I took the entire spray directly to the face.","\"...Mister.\"","\"Do mimics normally have legs?\"","Before Ludwig could answer my question—","\"ROOOOOAAAR!!!\"","The mimic, now sporting two arms and two legs, began crawling toward us like a wild beast.","Contrary to what I had been told about mimics being painfully slow, it charged at us with terrifying speed that rivaled a cheetah’s.","\"AAAAAAARGH!!!\"","\"Huhuhuhuhuh!\"","\"KYUAAAAARGH!!!\"","\"SCREEEEEECH!!!\"","For now, we ran.","Meanwhile, while the group was struggling inside the orichalcum cave—","\"Cheep! Cheep!\"","\"Cheep! Cheep!\"","\"Cheeeep! Cheep!\"","Outside the cave, Largo had been surrounded by chicks."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208","paragraphs":["There’s Space Behind the Pillar (2)","Contrary to what Ludwig had said, the mimic was extremely fast.","Having arms and legs was horrifying enough, but the way it crawled made it look like something straight out of a horror movie.","Even Ludwig seemed to have never seen anything like it before, judging by the dumbfounded laugh he let out.","\"Why?! Why are you only chasing me?!\"","\"ROOOAAAR!\"","It didn’t even glance at the others and relentlessly pursued me alone.","Maybe it was because I had disturbed it while it was sleeping, or perhaps because I was the only one overflowing with mana.","It could have been both. I shouted at Ludwig.","\"Mister! Do something!\"","At first, he had fled alongside me, but once the mimic began chasing only me, he stopped to take a breather.","At my urging, Ludwig stared blankly at the four-limbed mimic.","Then he picked up a chunk of orichalcum from the ground and hurled it.","Thud!","The orichalcum Ludwig threw struck the mimic’s leg.","The impact caused it to lose its balance and stagger.","This was my chance.","Slash!","While the mimic was stumbling, I spun around and swung my sword horizontally.","As I had mentioned, the mimic was crawling on all fours like a beast.","My horizontal slash neatly severed both of its arms, sending it crashing to the ground.","All that remained was to finish it off. Since that enormous tongue might still snatch me, I used aura for the finishing blow as well.","Stab!","I thrust my aura-clad sword through the slightly open lid.","The mimic’s tongue shot upright as though it had been startled.","Despite its terrifying appearance, I thought it might die easily.","\"...Gulp.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Gulp. Gulp.\"","The crazy bastard started gulping down my aura.","It wasn’t absorbing it like the guardian or a sponge, but the sight was still deeply unsettling.","However, thanks to my previous experience, I reacted without hesitation and used cold energy.","Crackle! Crack!","The mimic began freezing from the inside out. The rate at which it devoured my aura gradually slowed.","Eventually, its entire body froze solid, bringing its movements to a complete halt.","\"Phew...\"","I had been worried that even the cold might not work, but fortunately, that didn’t happen.","Once the others realized that the situation had been resolved, they gathered around one after another.","They all seemed fascinated by the four-limbed mimic and examined it from every angle.","Clatter!","\"Kyuaak!\"","\"Screech!\"","Despite being frozen all the way through, the mimic suddenly shook violently.","Apparently, it was still alive. We needed to finish it off properly.","We also needed to find out what had caused the mimic to glow.","To do that, we would have to stab around inside it with actual blades rather than aura.","\"Tyranno, can you use your breath?\"","\"Pii!\"","\"Mister, you know what to do once the ice melts, right?\"","Instead of answering, Ludwig gripped his mithril-orichalcum sword.","With that, all our preparations were complete. I told Kkobong to hold the mimic’s mouth open.","It might go berserk the moment the ice melted, so this was meant to prevent that.","\"Tyranno, do it now!\"","\"Pii!\"","Fwoosh!","A small burst of dragon breath erupted from Tyranno’s mouth.","Flames sometimes escaped from his mouth when he played with Wonmo, and seeing that had made me realize something.","Even a hatchling was still a dragon. He should have been capable of using dragon breath from a young age.","Hiss—","As the ice melted, the mimic began writhing more and more.","Fortunately, Kkobong was holding it firmly in place. Otherwise, it would have thrashed around wildly.","\"Now!\"","Once enough of the ice inside had melted, Ludwig and I thrust our swords into it at my signal.","We didn’t merely stab it. We completely tore up its insides.","\"Gueeeeh...\"","Only then did the mimic stop moving entirely.","Judging by its tongue hanging limply from its mouth, it was finally dead.","Its unexpected appearance had delayed us somewhat, but the subjugation itself had been relatively easy.","\"So what do we do now?\"","\"#96?\"","\"Doesn’t it spit everything out on its own?\"","I mimed pulling something out of my mouth as I questioned Ludwig.","Wasn’t a mimic supposed to vomit up everything inside it once it died?","Ludwig seemed to understand what I meant and kindly explained it to me.","\"#%#$%.\"","Unlike me, he mimed reaching his hand inside its mouth.","\"...\"","He was telling me we had to retrieve the treasure ourselves.","I immediately turned toward the mimic.","Its limp tongue was covered in thick, slimy saliva.","The inside of its mouth would undoubtedly be even worse.","Just imagining it made my skin crawl. I turned toward Ludwig.","\"...Rock-paper-scissors?\"","I discreetly held out my fist as I asked. I had no idea whether rock-paper-scissors existed in this world.","Had Ludwig understood what I wanted?","He stared at me for a moment, then pointed at my eyes.","He had no detection ability, whereas I did.","More importantly, I was the one who had suggested coming here. I should take responsibility for it.","Unable to argue, I eventually decided to retrieve the treasure myself.","Grimacing as hard as I could, I shoved my hand into the mimic’s mouth.","A sticky, unpleasant sensation traveled up my arm, accompanied by the slick touch of the mimic’s tongue.","’Please let it be something good...’","If I pulled out something useless, I would smash it on the spot.","I prayed desperately that I would receive a worthwhile reward for all my \"hard work.\"","After rummaging around for a while, my hand finally closed around something.","The instant I realized I had found an object, I pulled it out without hesitation.","\"Heave-ho!\"","The moment I yanked it free, the mimic’s saliva splattered across Ludwig’s face.","Let me make one thing clear: it was absolutely not intentional.","It had simply happened that way.","After apologizing to him, I examined the object that had been inside the mimic.","\"...What is this? A statue?\"","What I had retrieved from the mimic was some kind of statue—and an extraordinarily detailed one at that.","Although it was covered in saliva, its shape remained clearly distinguishable.","This was truly absurd.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","The statue was even glowing. So this really was what I had seen.","The question was, what exactly was this small statue, and why did it contain such tremendous mana?","’First, I should clean off the saliva.’","We had brought water with us, so I decided to wash away the saliva first.","I poured water over the statue and finally got a proper look at it.","The first thing I noticed was its thick suit of armor. Its appearance alone made it obvious that the figure was a knight.","It also had wings on its back and proudly held a massive shield before itself.","A helmet concealed its face, but even the helmet had been carved with exceptional precision.","The wings on its back and the enormous shield gave it an unmistakably extraordinary presence.","\"...Cain?\"","While I was examining the statue from different angles, Ludwig quietly muttered something.","When I looked at him, I found his eyes wide with surprise.","Judging by his reaction, he seemed to know whom the statue depicted.","\"Who did you say it was?\"","\"Cain.\"","\"Cain?\"","When I asked again, Ludwig nodded.","Apparently, the statue depicted someone named Cain.","Naturally, I had no idea who that was. I would have to ask the gallery.","’More importantly, what is this statue that makes it glow so brightly?’","It had been inside an orichalcum cave—and inside a mimic, no less.","It was clearly no ordinary statue. I should take it with me.","I placed the statue inside my spatial backpack and headed out. We had finished everything we needed to do in this cave.","All that remained was to return to the shelter. We didn’t bother taking the mimic with us.","I could purchase a chest through the gallery, and we had already squeezed everything of value out of the mimic.","When we finally emerged from the cave, we encountered an extraordinary scene.","\"Cluck, cluck!\"","\"Cheep! Cheep!\"","\"...\"","There was a chicken—the same one we had encountered before.","Behind it, countless chicks huddled together, chirping noisily.","That alone would have been absurd enough, but there was more.","\"Cluck! Cluck, cluck!\"","\"Grunt.\"","\"Cluck! Cluck-cluck!\"","The enormous black chicken was circling Largo as though performing a courtship display.","Largo himself merely wore a sullen expression.","The sight left me utterly dumbfounded.","’Judging by its comb, that chicken is male. Don’t tell me Largo is female?’","They weren’t even the same species.","Did species not matter as long as he found Largo attractive?","That was taking open-mindedness a little too far. I was speechless.","\"...Mister.\"","\"Mm.\"","\"Let’s get out of here.\"","We hurriedly fled.","Fortunately, Largo listened to us better than he did the chicken.","And so, we departed from the orichalcum cave.","\"COCK-A-DOODLE-DOO!!!\"","The chicken’s sorrowful roar echoed throughout the forest.","After returning to the shelter, I began by examining the statue in detail.","Its overall size was similar to that of a model kit or collectible figure.","The craftsmanship was so intricate that it looked as though it might come alive at any moment.","Moreover, it must have spent a very long time inside the mimic’s stomach.","Despite that, it remained perfectly intact, without a single damaged spot.","There was definitely something special about it.","’One thing’s certain: it contains tremendous mana.’","After pondering it briefly, I photographed the statue and uploaded the picture to the gallery.","Ludwig had called it Cain, so someone there would surely know who he was.","Title: Anyone Know Who Cain Is?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of Cain’s statue)","I got this after killing a mimic, and Ludwig says it’s Cain.","Does anyone know who Cain is?","└ Heavenly Demon: What an uncanny statue. It looks as though it might begin moving at any moment.","└ SwordMaster: A mimic? There are mimics in the Forest of Four Seasons too?","└ Wild Grylls: It was inside the orichalcum cave. But are mimics supposed to have arms and legs? This one even crawled around.","└ SwordMaster: I’ve never heard of such a grotesque mimic before...","└ Why would a mimic have arms and legs? Is that even anatomically possible?","└ Maybe it was an adult mimic or something?","└ Adult mimics live in places much larger than mere chests.","└ Where?","└ There have been cases where an entire cave was a mimic. They’re extremely rare, though.","└ Now we won’t even be able to enter caves without worrying, lol.","└ What if the cave Grylls lives in is actually a mimic?","└ Wild Grylls: Don’t say things like that. You’re making me nervous...","└ Starlight Princess: If it’s Cain, wouldn’t that be the first paladin? That’s what I was taught.","└ Wild Grylls: The first paladin?","└ Starlight Princess: Yes. He served as the shield of the goddess Ares. He was a figure who transcended legend and entered the realm of myth.","└ Wild Grylls: Then there must be a lot of statues of him.","└ Starlight Princess: Yes. There should be a statue of Cain in El Dorado’s capital right now.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I’ve read about him too! Lord Cain was also the first person to hold the title of Guardian! The most recent Guardian was Lord Ludwig!","└ But Ludwig is in the Forest of Four Seasons now, right?","└ Then who’s the Guardian right now?","└ No one. That’s why El Dorado has gone to hell.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: A new Guardian will appear someday!","To summarize, Cain was the first paladin as well as the first Guardian.","Ludwig had once held the title of El Dorado’s Guardian, so that alone demonstrated the magnitude of his reputation.","’This guy was incredibly important, wasn’t he?’","He had held the same title as someone who had transcended legend and entered the realm of myth.","Then again, El Dorado wouldn’t have been turned upside down by a single revelation if Ludwig hadn’t been someone of that stature.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: If you have no use for it, could you give it to me?!","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll have to see. It might be a little dangerous.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Dangerous?! It’s a statue carved in Lord Cain’s likeness! There’s no way it would harm anyone!","└ Wild Grylls: The very fact that it was in the Forest of Four Seasons is suspicious...","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Ah! That’s true! Then could you give it to me once you’re sure it’s safe?!","└ Wild Grylls: No. I’m going to sell it.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Don’t do thaaat!!!","└ A statue of that quality would sell for a fortune, lol.","└ It would probably be popular with collectors too.","└ But who made it? I’m starting to wonder.","└ Especially since it was hidden inside an orichalcum cave...","Well, if the opportunity arose, I might give it to the head moderator.","Keeping it here probably wouldn’t help me in any—","\"...\"","Or would it?","I looked toward Ludwig.","He was currently kneeling reverently before the statue and praying.","I didn’t know what he was praying for, but it was probably something along the lines of asking Cain to protect El Dorado.","\"...\"","’I should leave it here.’","Faith was essential to the devout, and Ludwig was an exceptionally faithful man.","Furthermore, faith could strengthen one’s resolve, so it would greatly aid his survival as well.","That didn’t mean I intended to pray, though.","I hated the gods because I didn’t want to hate people.","’Hey, your country is a complete mess. How about lending them a hand?’","Still, I could at least say a word for Ludwig’s sake.","Countless people wished for El Dorado to return to normal.","Once Ludwig finished praying, I spoke to him.","\"Mister, let’s get to work.\"","Work still had to be done.","***","Grylls left the cave with Ludwig and all the animals.","It was almost time to prepare their meal, and there were also a few things he needed to inspect carefully.","Consequently, Cain’s statue was left alone inside the cave.","Until then, the statue had shown no reaction whatsoever.","Flicker—","Amazingly, light suddenly shone from the eye slits of its helmet.","Then it began murmuring something.","\"...the call...\"","\"...shall...\"","\"...answer...\"","Click—","The moment the statue finished speaking, the light vanished."]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209","paragraphs":["Winter Has Come (1)","While Grylls and Ludwig were making thorough preparations for the approaching winter, the rest of the world was passing through an extremely turbulent period filled with all manner of incidents.","The greatest turmoil of all was unfolding in El Dorado.","Contrary to predictions that Ludwig’s revelations would spark a civil war, the citizens focused solely on protesting.","There were two primary reasons for this.","The first was the absence of a central figure.","Protesters tended to become disorganized without a leader to take charge of the situation.","The more unstable the political climate, the more desperately they needed a charismatic leader. However, no such figure had emerged yet.","Furthermore, the citizens of El Dorado possessed an exceptional degree of patriotism and pride in their homeland.","For centuries, they had served as the sword and shield of Ares, fighting demon kings and their demonic forces.","The sense of duty that came from fighting an unmistakable \"evil\" had allowed El Dorado to develop into a great power.","Under such circumstances, were they supposed to start a civil war that would tear their homeland apart?","No one could readily bring themselves to take that step.","The second reason was their lack of military strength.","In truth, this was the greatest reason of all.","El Dorado’s military was currently held firmly in the grasp of Pope Louis II.","With Ludwig and most of those associated with him having been purged, virtually no one remained except the pope’s puppets.","No matter how proud or patriotic the citizens might be, such feelings did not automatically translate into military power. They could not hope to match a professionally trained army.","Above all, the citizens firmly believed that the army existed to defeat external enemies, not the people it was meant to protect.","As long as the soldiers did not regard them as \"enemies,\" they believed the army would never turn its blades upon them.","Title: The Protests in El Dorado Are Fundamentally Different","Most protests usually happen because people feel they can’t survive anymore.","The economy has completely collapsed, there’s a famine, or a war has pushed them to their absolute limit.","But the protests in El Dorado are driven purely by anger and a sense of betrayal toward the leadership.","Honestly, it doesn’t matter whether those in power have bizarre fetishes or strange hobbies as long as they govern the country properly.","The upper and lower classes are strictly separated anyway. A few commoners occasionally enter politics, but they’re a tiny minority.","The protesters can unite like this—and avoid crossing the line—precisely because they’re driven purely by anger and betrayal toward the leadership.","└ They just don’t have any power. If they did, they would’ve overthrown the government ages ago, lol.","└ If Ludwig were still there, he probably would’ve torn the whole thing down, lol.","└ What has the pope been saying lately, anyway? Has he said anything?","└ He says never to believe the groundless rumors spreading through the gallery. Apparently, Ludwig is also a man who committed a grave crime.","└ He still hasn’t come to his senses. Does anyone actually believe that?","└ Surprisingly, a shitload of people do. All the cardinals say the pope is right.","└ That’s because they’re all his bootlickers...","└ The army isn’t going to massacre the protesters, right?","└ Maybe if it were a riot or rebellion, but this is an ordinary protest. Doing that would be insane.","└ Word would spread all over the gallery. How could they possibly stop the information from getting out?","└ Seems like they’ve been laying the groundwork for that. They keep telling the media that an evil entity is operating behind the scenes.","└ Is that \"evil entity\" supposed to be Grylls?","└ They haven’t said it outright, but it’s almost certainly him. They’re calling the protesters a faction that supports the Immortal King.","└ Meanwhile, the survivors of the Balkan Kingdom curse the Immortal King every chance they get, lol.","└ There are survivors from the Balkan Kingdom?","└ They’ve been incorporated into El Dorado, but their territory still exists.","└ Wild Grylls: Why me?","└ Oh, Grylls. Congratulations. Looks like you’ll become a Demon King soon.","└ Wild Grylls: ??? What the hell are you talking about?","└ The pope says he’ll brand you a Demon King if you keep this up, lol.","└ Louis: You’re a Demon King now.","└ Wild Grylls: Good grief, lol. Tell him I wouldn’t take that tiny-ass country even if he gave it to me.","└ Then what country would you want besides El Dorado?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t want any of them. I just want to go home.","└ Aren’t you already home?","└ Exactly. Why does he keep saying he wants to go home when he’s already there?","└ Wild Grylls: F—","Title: Still, It’s a Fact That This Is Worrying","What bothers me most is that the pope keeps issuing warnings.","He says he won’t stand idly by if the protesters refuse to back down.","He says they’re being deceived and have fallen under sorcery even more wicked than necromancy.","He isn’t going to declare it a riot and send in the army, is he?","└ Wouldn’t the other countries condemn him if he did?","└ What could they do besides condemn him? If El Dorado insists it’s a rebellion or riot... Another country’s intervention could start a war.","└ Would they really tell such an obvious lie when the gallery exists? Lol.","└ Plenty of people only see what they want to see, even with the gallery around.","└ Once people become trapped in the belief that whatever they see must be the truth, there’s no helping them.","└ What is the Hero doing? If the Hero intervened now, they might be able to reach some kind of compromise.","└ It would only make things worse if the Hero sided with the protesters. The pope would seize the opportunity to declare it a rebellion.","└ The pope might be getting cursed to hell right now, but that doesn’t mean the Hero is no longer considered a traitor.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: The Hero isn’t a traitor! It’s all a misunderstanding!","└ Yeah, we know, but how is she supposed to clear her name?","└ Everyone who matters already knows, Head Mod. The situation is just completely fucked.","└ Every time I see something like this, I’m reminded that the pope is disgustingly good at politics, lol.","└ The bitter part is that he only bothers with politics when he needs to preserve his own power...","While the situation in El Dorado gradually took a sinister turn, the Hero, Asella, was silently making her way toward the capital with Reina.","Along the way, she also managed the gallery and monitored the situation.","As they neared their intended destination, Reina, who was riding ahead, spoke.","\"What are you thinking about?\"","\"...Is it really okay for us to do this?\"","They were currently riding horses.","Naturally, the horses had not been acquired through any legal procedure.","Then where had they obtained them?","\"What’s the problem? It’s not as if I said anything untrue.\"","\"I’m not a wanted criminal...\"","\"I don’t think you are either. The authorities would disagree, though. Would you rather I call you a traitor?\"","\"I-I’d hate that even more!\"","The situation had unfolded roughly as follows.","While they were being pursued by trackers, Reina had suggested turning the tables on their pursuers.","The upright Asella naturally refused, but Reina relentlessly pushed the idea.","Most of the pursuit teams traveled using horses or similar means of transportation.","In that case, there were bound to be grooms responsible for caring for those animals.","If they found and threatened the grooms, they could secure transportation for themselves.","\"Hey, friends. Is anyone among you armed or wanted by the Holy Kingdom?\"","\"Uh, no...\"","\"We’re both.\"","\"...\"","\"So you understand, right?\"","When Reina threatened them along those lines, the grooms obediently produced two horses.","It was the art of obtaining exactly what she wanted without shedding a single drop of blood.","Asella couldn’t understand Reina, but she decided to let it go.","Her beloved homeland was in danger. This was no time to be particular about their methods.","\"How far are we from the capital?\"","\"Two days if we take it easy. If we’re lucky, we might arrive tonight.\"","Although Asella was being pursued, she had not fled to another country.","Escaping abroad required the use of illegal routes, and Asella knew nothing about such things.","Consequently, she had been wandering in circles around El Dorado, particularly near the capital.","There was a reason Reina had found her so quickly.","\"I wish we could go faster...\"","\"No. We’ll exhaust the horses. We don’t even have anything to feed them.\"","\"Couldn’t we continue on foot?\"","\"You might be able to, but my knees ache too much.\"","’You’re only two years older than me.’","Asella grumbled inwardly.","However, Reina was right. They had no fodder for the horses, so prolonged travel would be difficult.","They needed to conserve their stamina by riding as far as possible, then continue on foot if necessary.","\"Are you that worried?\"","\"...Yes.\"","Asella nodded gravely in response to Reina’s question.","Unlike the gallery, where people discussed all kinds of theories, the newspapers continued to focus on the protests.","No matter how important the gallery might be, it could never take precedence over reality. The same was true for Asella.","The protests in El Dorado were also why she had recently failed to fulfill her duties as head moderator.","\"Don’t worry too much. If the pope can’t endure the pressure, he’ll step down on his own.\"","\"Will... he?\"","Despite Reina’s optimistic words, Asella couldn’t shake her anxiety.","Would that pope truly surrender his position voluntarily?","The same man who had orchestrated a massive purge?","Furthermore, a rumor occasionally surfaced in the gallery: the pope was currently mobilizing the army.","What possible role could the army serve under these circumstances?","Without realizing it, Asella began imagining the worst possible outcome.","’Paladins are Lady Ares’s sword and shield. Would they turn that sword and shield against the citizens...?’","That would never happen.","If Ares learned of such a deed, she would surely be furious.","’But if they really intend to do that...’","What was she supposed to do?","Asella continued wrestling with the question.","She still had no answer by the time they reached El Dorado.","***","As Reina and Asella gradually drew closer to El Dorado, the papal administration was preparing a large-scale operation.","Only a limited number of organizations ordinarily used the word \"operation.\"","The foremost example was the embodiment of a nation’s armed might:","The military.","\"As you have all heard, the protesters are currently afflicted by the Immortal King’s wicked curse.\"","The briefing began with the commander’s plausible-sounding bullshit.","The problem was that every soldier present sincerely believed it.","The paladins listening to the operation wore tense or resolute expressions.","They clearly perceived the protesters outside as people afflicted by a curse.","There had been relentless indoctrination and an endless stream of lies. Above all, the military was largely a closed organization.","When people absorbed nothing but the stories circulating within an isolated environment, certain \"beliefs\" naturally took root.","\"We must stop them. As the sword and shield of Ares, it is our duty to protect El Dorado.\"","Protect our homeland.","Those words alone would inspire a sense of duty.","The problem was that the \"citizens\" had been excluded from that homeland.","The paladins failed to recognize that contradiction.","One might wonder how anyone could close the paladins’ eyes and ears when the gallery openly existed.","However, the gallery had always been notorious for its lack of credibility.","They were told that the gallery itself had been corrupted by the Immortal King’s curse and that nothing said there was true.","Moreover, the Immortal King incident thirty years ago had been so horrific that such a claim did not seem entirely impossible.","As these numerous factors accumulated, the military gradually came to perceive the protesters as its enemy.","\"We will begin by repeatedly warning the protesters. The clergy will continue attempting to dispel the curse.\"","The protesters were not cursed.","They were merely overwhelmed by betrayal and anger.","Those were natural human emotions, yet the authorities dismissed them as a curse.","\"If the curse cannot be broken...\"","The commander paused, then sighed as though the prospect genuinely pained him.","\"We will have no choice but to break it ourselves.\"","The sweltering heat of summer was currently approaching El Dorado.","\"You are the heroes capable of saving El Dorado. Is that understood?\"","\"Yes, sir!!!\"","Yet this summer seemed destined to become a bitterly cold season.","Meanwhile, in the Forest of Four Seasons—","\"...What are you doing here?\"","\"Snort.\"","Grylls, who was likewise preparing for a bitterly cold winter, encountered an unexpected visitor.","It looked like an ordinary deer, but its familiar cynical expression told him they had met before.","The deer was holding an apple in its mouth.","Amazingly, the apple glittered with a golden light.","It wasn’t shining because of the light reflected in Grylls’s eyes. The apple itself was a gleaming golden color.","It looked exactly like a golden apple from mythology, leaving Grylls thoroughly bewildered.","\"Moo. Moo.\"","\"Cold days coming. Give me fire. Like last time. Then I give you this.\"","\"...You want me to light a fire for you?\"","\"Mooo.\"","Through Kkobong, the animal interpreter, Grylls was able to understand what the deer was saying.","After considering its request for a moment, Grylls turned his head.","In that direction stood the brick house they had labored so hard to build.","\"...Do you want to live in there over the winter?\"","\"Moo.\"","Plop—","Once Grylls gave his permission, the deer dropped the golden apple.","A strange winter was approaching."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210","paragraphs":["Winter Has Come (2)","The deer that brought the golden apple was treated as a guest rather than a member of the family.","All the deer needed was a warm fire.","So I let it stay in the brick house. Kkobong was initially on high alert, but it wasn’t long before he lowered his guard.","After all, Kkobong was weak when he couldn’t use mana.","Perhaps the deer knew that, or maybe it was simply displaying its usual composure. Either way, it didn’t seem concerned.","The day after we accepted the deer as our guest—","\"Haah...\"","I stared at the cave entrance, which had been completely buried beneath the snow, and sighed.","\"It’s finally here.\"","The cold season—winter—had arrived.","***","It hadn’t rained yesterday, but the weather had become bitterly cold, so I had already suspected this would happen.","That was why we had kept the fireplace burning to prevent the chimney from becoming blocked.","Fast Sloth was constantly adding firewood anyway, so there was no danger of the fire going out.","Even so, we couldn’t simply leave the cave entrance buried beneath the snow.","We also needed to check the condition of the house next door—the brick house where the animals lived.","\"Mister, aren’t you cold—\"","\"Grrrrr...\"","Perhaps it was thanks to the cold-weather clothing we had received from the dwarf, or maybe it was the fireplace’s comforting warmth.","Despite ordinarily waking early like a proper soldier, Ludwig was still snoring.","Well, it was six in the morning, so I couldn’t blame him.","’Wonmo has gone into hibernation, but what about Tyranno?’","Wonmo had entered hibernation after growing plump with fur and fat.","I wasn’t sure about Tyranno, though. He might resemble a reptile, but he was still a dragon. Perhaps he didn’t need to hibernate.","In any case, clearing the snow came first.","I used the emergency exit I had constructed for situations like this.","Like a chimney, the emergency exit extended through the ceiling and consisted of a long passageway.","I had built it in preparation for the possibility of the snow accumulating to an abnormal depth.","I had even made the roof sloped.","However, constructing a proper hatch had been difficult, so I had been forced to cover the opening with multiple layers of cloth.","\"Heave-ho.\"","I climbed the ladder inside the passageway and emerged outside.","The moment I stepped out, I felt the bitterly cold air.","The entire forest was also covered in pure white snow.","It had been the same last time. Whenever winter arrived, snow piled up everywhere.","’Fortunately, the brick house hasn’t collapsed.’","Although some snow had accumulated on its roof, the house remained intact.","Smoke was rising from the chimney, so Kkobong must have been feeding the fire.","Now that I had roughly assessed the situation, all that remained was the actual work.","\"Mister, wake up.\"","\"Mmm...\"","Ludwig staggered to his feet and joined me.","Upon emerging from the passageway, his mouth fell open at the sight of the enormous amount of snow.","He probably hadn’t expected so much to accumulate in a single night.","Still, it had to be done. I handed him a shovel.","\"Let’s clear it.\"","\"...$%%$#.\"","I think he called it \"garbage that fell from the sky.\"","I wholeheartedly agreed.","Why did garbage like this have to fall from the sky?","The snow itself was bad enough, but the real hell would begin once it froze and turned the ground into an icy death trap.","Crackle! Pop!","As we cleared the snow, we also built campfires here and there.","The last thing we needed to do was inspect the inside of the brick house.","Its entrance had also been buried beneath the snow, and since the building had no windows, there was no way to see inside.","When I finally entered—","\"Zzzzz...\"","Everyone was sleeping peacefully.","The deer that had arrived as a guest was no exception.","The fireplace must have been exceptionally effective, because the interior was filled with cozy warmth.","\"Hey, wake up. It’s time for breakfast.\"","\"Grunt?\"","Only then did the animals begin to stir at my voice.","The deer raised its head after hearing me, but soon let it droop again.","It appeared to assume that it wouldn’t receive any food because it was merely a guest.","\"Hey, long-neck.\"","\"Grunt?\"","\"Not you.\"","Right. There was someone here with an even longer neck.","I was calling the deer, not Largo.","The deer stared at me with a frown, as though asking why I had called it.","\"Do you want breakfast too? You’ll be staying here all winter anyway.\"","\"...Moo.\"","The deer lowered its head again as though declining.","Then it settled into an extremely comfortable sleeping position.","Deer and other herbivores ordinarily curled up when they slept.","This deer did nothing of the sort. It sprawled out as though it were relaxing in its own bedroom.","’If it says it’ll find its own food, then whatever.’","There was no need for me to prepare anything separately.","Furthermore, the deer wasn’t originally from this part of the forest.","It had most likely come here because it wanted somewhere warm to spend the winter.","The fact that it had personally brought a golden apple I had never seen anywhere else made that obvious.","\"Master. What food?\"","\"Wild boar meat and sweet potatoes.\"","Since Wonmo was hibernating, we had plenty of food.","After enjoying a hearty breakfast, I returned to the cave.","There was almost nothing worthwhile to do during winter.","At most, there was training and gathering Ice Flowers.","I would have liked to gain resistance to cold from the Ice Flowers, but—","’I’m afraid I’ll acquire another bizarre ability.’","It would be better to discuss that with Starlight Princess gradually.","For now, there was something else I wanted to investigate before the Ice Flowers.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","I held the golden apple that the deer had brought late last night.","It gleamed as though covered in gold leaf.","Golden apples appeared frequently in mythology, and this one was about the size of an ordinary apple.","’Where in the world did it find something like this?’","First the honey-filled beehive, and now a golden apple.","Whenever the deer visited my shelter, it brought remarkably rare objects with it.","I didn’t know whether it possessed some special ability or simply lived near a place where such treasures could be found.","’First, I should ask what effects it has.’","I immediately connected to the gallery.","Title: I Got a Golden Apple","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the deer sleeping comfortably inside the brick house)","(Photo of the glittering golden apple)","The deer that gave me honey last time gave me a golden apple this time.","It asked me to let it sleep in the brick house in exchange for the apple.","I accepted it, but does anyone know what this thing does? It looks amazing at first glance.","└ Heavenly Demon: What an appetizing apple.","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t golden apples something from mythology? I heard that eating one grants extraordinary abilities.","└ Heavenly Demon: What sort of abilities?","└ SwordMaster: Most stories say they restore youth. Since you’re from the Central Plains, Heavenly Demon, you know about the Herb of Immortality, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: I have heard it is a medicinal herb that grants eternal life to those who consume it.","└ SwordMaster: Some stories claim the Herb of Immortality is actually the cotyledon of the tree that bears golden apples.","└ Why do you know so much about this?","└ May I ask how old you are...?","└ SwordMaster: Shut up.","└ Heavenly Demon: This one does not find it particularly enticing. What do you intend to do with it?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll eat it first and think about that afterward. If I get more later, I’ll share them with you.","└ All-Father: If that truly is the golden apple of myth... Forgive my impertinence, but could you give me even its peel?","└ The professor is back again, lol.","└ You know it’s genuine when he’s begging for even the peel, lmao.","└ Does the peel have an effect too?","└ It probably isn’t completely ineffective.","└ Wild Grylls: I can certainly give you the peel. Does it have any effects besides restoring youth?","└ All-Father: According to the literature, its symbolic significance outweighs its practical effects. Golden apples frequently appeared as gifts exchanged between the gods.","So golden apples appeared in this world’s mythology too.","How fascinating.","In any case, eating it would probably be best. I wanted to share it with the named users, but there simply wasn’t enough.","Unlike the golden mushrooms, whose effects could be either extremely beneficial or catastrophically harmful, the golden apple appeared to have nothing but positive effects.","’They say an apple in the morning is good for you, right?’","I slowly began peeling the apple with my dagger.","The flesh underneath shone even more brilliantly than its skin.","My mouth was already watering. Its effects aside, I was curious about how it tasted.","\"Here. Have a slice.\"","\"Thank you.\"","\"You have some too, Fast Sloth. Tyranno, you too.\"","\"Pii!\"","I divided the apple into eight slices and handed them out.","I even forcibly woke the hibernating Wonmo and put a piece in his mouth.","Crunch, crunch—","\"Oh.\"","\"$%.\"","\"Pii!\"","It was sweet.","That was the first thought that entered my mind the instant I bit into it.","Despite having no honey on it, a rich sweetness and fragrance filled my mouth.","I was incredibly curious about where the deer had found this golden apple.","’As for its effects... I can’t really tell.’","Despite its brilliant glow, my mana had not increased by any noticeable amount.","Of course, that might have been because I already possessed an enormous amount of mana.","It would be better to examine Ludwig’s reaction.","\"Mist—\"","The moment I saw Ludwig’s face, I froze.","As befitted someone of his tremendous ability, Ludwig possessed an exceptionally high affinity for mana.","That would ordinarily delay the aging process, but he was a soldier—a soldier who had survived countless battles.","Since he had never undergone bodily reformation, he had accumulated wrinkles like an ordinary person and bore every mark of the hardships he had endured.","\"...Who are you?\"","But look at him now.","The seasoned veteran who had been sitting there moments earlier had vanished.","A few wrinkles remained, but he looked at least ten years younger.","Ludwig himself continued chewing the apple as though he hadn’t noticed any change.","Surely he should at least have noticed the changes in his own body.","\"Mister, look in the mirror.\"","\"?\"","I kindly handed him a mirror.","Ludwig looked puzzled at first, but the moment he saw his reflection, his eyes widened.","He repeatedly examined himself, running his hands over his face.","\"...Oh?\"","That was all he said.","His reaction suggested that even he hadn’t expected this.","He then stretched and loosened his muscles to assess his physical condition.","Just as his face had grown younger, his entire body appeared to have been rejuvenated. His joints seemed to move even more smoothly than before.","’His foot is still the same.’","Regardless of his restored youth, his mithril foot remained unchanged.","If Ludwig had become younger, what about the animals?","I checked Fast Sloth first.","I couldn’t identify any visible changes. The same applied to Tyranno and Wonmo.","Apparently, those who were still growing or whose bodies were already at their physical prime were exceptions.","’Or perhaps it extends the duration of their prime?’","That led me to another thought.","’Don’t tell me that deer has been eating golden apples regularly.’","Its youthful appearance contrasted sharply with its constant composure, and it possessed tremendous strength as well.","Perhaps it was far older than I imagined.","After briefly considering that possibility, I checked the remaining apple slices.","Despite sharing it with everyone except the deer and the raccoon family, one slice remained.","’The deer said it didn’t need any, and the raccoon family declined.’","Who should I give this last slice to?","As I considered the question, someone suddenly came to mind.","SwordMaster, the named user who had always been unusually sensitive about youth.","She would probably appreciate it.","’But first, I should send the apple peel to All-Father.’","Afterward, I immediately sent SwordMaster a private message.","[SwordMaster: You’re giving me a slice of the apple?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I happened to have one left, and you seemed to want it.]","[SwordMaster: When did I ever say that?]","[Wild Grylls: You didn’t? Then I’ll give it to someone else.]","[SwordMaster: W-Wait a momemt!]","She must have panicked badly enough to make a typo. I chuckled.","[SwordMaster: Just so we’re clear, I’m not some old hag. Understood?]","[Wild Grylls: I wouldn’t insult someone who has helped me.]","[SwordMaster: You even have a wonderful personality. Hurry up and marry me.]","[Wild Grylls: If you’re willing to wait until I escape from here.]","By now, I could respond to jokes like that with jokes of my own.","After receiving the golden apple slice, SwordMaster thanked me repeatedly.","’I should ask the deer where it found the apple later.’","Perhaps it was because the winter cold was so bitter.","The rest of the day passed peacefully, with nothing in particular to do.","***","Meanwhile, Ash—SwordMaster—had received a slice of golden apple as a gift from Grylls.","\"...Oh, for fuck’s sake.\"","She cursed upon witnessing the golden apple’s astonishing effects.","Why would she curse if its effects were so beneficial?","A glance at her bed would provide the answer.","Ash already had the appearance of a woman in her mid-twenties, so the golden apple held little significance for her.","She had also recently eaten the honey she received from Grylls, leaving even her skin smooth and flawless.","Consequently, she had eaten the golden apple simply because receiving it put her in a good mood.","Clack—","\"Dear, what are you—hm?\"","The problem was Ash’s innate talent.","Her talent was so exceptional that even calling it heaven-sent seemed insufficient.","Her swordsmanship talent was extraordinary, but her physical gifts were especially absurd.","\"Ash?\"","\"Yes, it’s me.\"","\"You look... younger.\"","Ash’s mother asked in a bewildered voice.","Her reaction was perfectly understandable.","Just as a newly blossomed flower was at its most beautiful, a woman’s beauty was said to shine most brightly when it first came into bloom.","In Ash’s case, that had been when she was exactly eighteen.","She remembered receiving countless marriage proposals at that age.","Her mother remembered that period vividly and therefore recognized it better than anyone.","Ash was also exceptionally tall for a woman, which made her beauty stand out even more.","\"Yes. Well...\"","Ash was widely regarded as the strongest swordswoman on the continent.","\"This is what happened.\"","And now she had undergone an entirely unwanted return to youth.","’Actually, this isn’t bad at all.’","Contrary to her initial outburst, she was extremely satisfied.","She hadn’t simply become prettier. She had genuinely grown younger.","’At this point, maybe age doesn’t matter anymore.’","Ash began entertaining pleasant fantasies.","While someone in a distant corner of the continent underwent an unwanted return to youth—","\"We’re here.\"","\"...We are.\"","Asella, the Hero, arrived at the capital.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]}]);
